.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, but that doesn't mean that every Fenrir or Talons sept will do it. Look at Golgol Fangs First, or the one from Wind Catchers sept from Chicago, the oldest Gets I remember. As for other tribes I don't know how many old Garou they have. The only exception IMHO, are Shadow Lords. They are known for their ability of using every resources they can lay their hands on. So I believe that, considering their elders, they will let them live and fight the Wyrm to the end... without any support of course. I also believe that they could arrange an agreement with Skin Dancers and use their rite as some kind of &quot;recycling&quot;. They could use the BSDs skins (or their fallen camerades), choose a promising Kinfolk and allow him to become Garou. It's a win-win situation: they give a sign for their Kinfolks &quot;be loyal and you could be rewarded&quot;, can replenish their ranks, and, as those Kinfolk will likely make Wyrm Sense tingling and they will be the only ones who know the truth, assure their loyalty (no to mention that they know the dark secrets of their new members). I run a story like that once, but I use a Children of Gaia with a practical mind and it was interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1423901#post1423901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From a Garou perspective, that is not her only sin. First, most Garou would not think she was overprotective at all. They would think she was <i>harming</i> her own child because to be a Garou is a great, great thing. There is no way most septs (who knows, maybe the Bone Gnawers) would allow the argument that she spared her child how &quot;awful&quot; it is to be Garou. They think being Garou is awesome. And as a dying people engaged at the height of a brutal struggle to save Gaia, this Theurge is purposefully sabotaging the Nation as a whole by preventing one of Gaia's protectors from assuming his place. Then of course would be the crime of abusing a Rite of Protection by using it in an inproper fashion. So there's several crimes she's committed.<br /> <br /> The typical suspects - Children of Gaia and Bone Gnawers - may mitigate the punishment, but I think most tribes would deal with her very harshly. Some would likely execute her as a traitor and use the rite of Gaia's Vengeful Teeth (again the other usual suspects here - Red Talons and Get of Fenris among them, but probably the other traditionalists as well). Others may just kill her without using the rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I can agree with most parts, except the one about seeing Garou's life as glorious. In my World of Darkness most of them are bitter and pathetic creatures, often despising each other. They know that they are losing the war and it can be seen. But in a world like that, when my players would meet mentioned mother they would likely die in her defence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1423901#post1423901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the PCs who have been in my games (that I either run or play in for tabletop), I would say I'd expect something like 10% to be against killing the Theurge, 30% agreeing but feel bad doing so and agonizing over the decision to various degrees during a roleplay scene, and the other 60% swiftly agreeing on her punishment. I think almost all PCs would agree IC that the Theurge was objectively wrong - its just whether they consider the punishment to be mitigated in any way. As for my PCs that I play, it'd probably be almost 100% who'd kill her as I usually play very traditional Garou who don't fit with modern human sensibilities. There's certainly valid PC concepts that would react differently. As an ST, I could see NPCs that are against it especially certain tribes and certain septs with certain types of caern types. I imagine other gaming groups as a whole would split more evenly. In certain large scale LARPs and online games, it might break more 40/60 or 50/50. The larger the game, the more likely players will roleplay with 21st century Western values and wimp out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I know certain PCs in my games that not only would kill the Theurge for her crimes, but would probably want to kill the NPC that made this argument in her defense. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They would say this stinks of cowardice and defeatism. While they wouldn't kill the NPC who argued this, they would probably keep an eye on them or even mark them out for future reprisals in some fashion. They'd be looking for an opportunity to kill (or at least harm) when it would be justified. That's how angry the argument would make them. They might even ask if they need to make Rage rolls to prevent Frenzy.<br /> <br /> That's outside of any OOC discussion whether that character was objectively right or wrong in their evaluation of the Garou's war or the state of their nation. I know plenty of players who might agree themselves, but their PC act differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhhh, yes, I forgot. Most players will deal harshly with NPCs (when you run a story like that during your game), but they will not harm other player's character even if they could, should or even have to (like during LARPs). My observations are the same. I remember one LARP, when the Warder allowed a BSD messenger enter the Caern (he came with a white flag, but IMHO that doesn't change anything) and traded a Fetish taken from BSD a century ago for lives of a Sept Leader and 4 other Garou taken as hostages by BSD pack. Later he allowed (he was a kind of a leader's deputy) the leader to enter the Caern freely. And only I started to called him -ikhtya (I played Ragabash, so my character didn't frenzy). Instead of tearing my head off (as an Ahroun should) he warned me 3 times before challenging me for a duel. I lost, but still was happy. That's why I love to use my other players as First Mates for the most important NPCs. My players don't know it they are new players or not, so the moral choices are harder.<br /> <br /> And thank you for your appreciation \ud83d\ude42.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-15-2020, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T02:03:03-08:00","id":1424209,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't reflect on all the stuff above this, couse it's huge, and I usualy agree with Black Fox.<br /> <br /> Some ideas:<br /> 1) About the non-metis child. The only thing what came to my mind could be long-lost gifts/rites of Apis. Still they job was not to breed against the will of Gaia.<br /> No Umbral realm (only some homebrew) would let the Garou parents breed a non-Metis.<br /> And really why would they breed? This goes clearly against the Litany and they sould be hit with much dis-renown for the deed, even if they succeed.<br /> The role of ragabash is not to violate every sacred and (in this case) accepted tradition.<br /> 2) About the theurge: As a storyteller I would not let the rite succeed as the child was not guilty. The rites are empowered by the spirits and they have all the right to say &quot;hack no!&quot;. Check W20 Core; pg. 214. On my table she would loss many Honor and Wisdom additionaly.<br /> 3) Skin Dancers: They become (mechanicaly) Garou. Gnosis/Rage/Gifts are all aspects, but not the whole picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T08:26:50-08:00","id":1424276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424209#post1424209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't reflect on all the stuff above this, couse it's huge, and I usualy agree with Black Fox.<br /> <br /> Some ideas:<br /> 1) About the non-metis child. The only thing what came to my mind could be long-lost gifts/rites of Apis. Still they job was not to breed against the will of Gaia.<br /> No Umbral realm (only some homebrew) would let the Garou parents breed a non-Metis.<br /> And really why would they breed? This goes clearly against the Litany and they sould be hit with much dis-renown for the deed, even if they succeed.<br /> The role of ragabash is not to violate every sacred and (in this case) accepted tradition.<br /> 2) About the theurge: As a storyteller I would not let the rite succeed as the child was not guilty. The rites are empowered by the spirits and they have all the right to say &amp;quot;hack no!&amp;quot;. Check W20 Core; pg. 214. On my table she would loss many Honor and Wisdom additionaly.<br /> 3) Skin Dancers: They become (mechanicaly) Garou. Gnosis/Rage/Gifts are all aspects, but not the whole picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The question is not why but why not. Some Garou fall in love with each other, I can understand their desire of having children and I can imagine that they would rather want a healthy one. As for Apis I've heard about them but I don't know the details. In case of some umbral land that could possibly allow that is the Summer Country. I remember from 1st Edition of Umbra: the Velvet Shadow that in Summer Country metis deformities can be healed so I believe that metis born there could be free of them. Of course first you have to get there. As for Ragabashes I know that they purpose is not violating ever taboo. But still there are extremists. Or hungry for glory. Or even the stupid ones.<br /> 2. Then what about Rites which are used unjustfully? Or, using the dices language, botched? I would still allow it. The consequences are another thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T12:19:03-08:00","id":1424326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424276#post1424276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. The question is not why but why not. Some Garou fall in love with each other, I can understand their desire of having children and I can imagine that they would rather want a healthy one. As for Apis I've heard about them but I don't know the details. In case of some umbral land that could possibly allow that is the Summer Country. I remember from 1st Edition of Umbra: the Velvet Shadow that in Summer Country metis deformities can be healed so I believe that metis born there could be free of them. Of course first you have to get there. As for Ragabashes I know that they purpose is not violating ever taboo. But still there are extremists. Or hungry for glory. Or even the stupid ones.<br /> 2. Then what about Rites which are used unjustly? Or, using the dices language, botched? I would still allow it. The consequences are another thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. There is a vast difference between two humans wanting a child and two garou wanting a child. First of all, unless we are talking about BSDs, no canon metis has ever been a wanted child. The common narrative of them, troubling or not, is that their parents fooled around and broke up after the female got pregnant. Then at best they give the metis away or worst they have to raise the child themselves. Neither option is ever treated as anything but difficult. Plus there is the thing, garou KNOW that a metis will ALWAYS be significantly disabled and sterile. Most likely will kill the mother and then live a life of constant judgement. This is a given, not a maybe. No parent wants their child to suffer like that, so why risk it?<br /> <br /> Besides, garou are a dying race. Despite what Changing Ways says, it is much better to have non-metis garou to fill the numbers. This is something told to cubs from day one of their training. That is why kinfolk are so put upon, because they are the breeding stock/meal-tickets. Those who try to keep garou mates are usually either not into the whole Nation thing or are just venting out their frustrations with each other.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2. There is a difference between thinking someone is guilty and abusing the rite's effects. The former can happen, the latter is insulting for the spirits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T14:25:56-08:00","id":1424353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424326#post1424326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. There is a vast difference between two humans wanting a child and two garou wanting a child. First of all, unless we are talking about BSDs, no canon metis has ever been a wanted child. The common narrative of them, troubling or not, is that their parents fooled around and broke up after the female got pregnant. Then at best they give the metis away or worst they have to raise the child themselves. Neither option is ever treated as anything but difficult. Plus there is the thing, garou KNOW that a metis will ALWAYS be significantly disabled and sterile. Most likely will kill the mother and then live a life of constant judgement. This is a given, not a maybe. No parent wants their child to suffer like that, so why risk it?<br /> <br /> Besides, garou are a dying race. Despite what Changing Ways says, it is much better to have non-metis garou to fill the numbers. This is something told to cubs from day one of their training. That is why kinfolk are so put upon, because they are the breeding stock/meal-tickets. Those who try to keep garou mates are usually either not into the whole Nation thing or are just venting out their frustrations with each other.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2. There is a difference between thinking someone is guilty and abusing the rite's effects. The former can happen, the latter is insulting for the spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Why are you all so obessed with killing? Remember, Metis or not, he's still a Garou. And not all old and disabled are eliminated. I remember an NPC from &quot;Caerns: Places of Power&quot;, from Get of Fenris Schwartzwald caern, who was attacked and horribly deformed by Tzimisce and yet they allow her to live. In one of the harshest caerns in the world. You are also right about Garou being a dying race. That's why more and more Metis are allowed to live. Their parents too. And that's why I also had a Ragabash NPC who, inspired by Sabbat Mass Embraces, stated that every Garou, regardless of race, should bring at least one Metis to this world (to buy Gaia some time), mate with a wolf (with more children from one pregnancy chances for Garou are bigger) then move to mate with his proper race. Besides I know that every two Garou union ends with a Metis child. I rather try to find a relatively easy way to avoid that. Easy enough to be worth a try, hard enough to be an exception and not destroy the setting.<br /> <br /> 2. Of course, it's a big difference. But, as it was said in p. ex. Storyteller's Handbook spirits can be bargained with, can be bribed or even made to do something the ritemaster wants. And I doubt that even an insult to the spirit will be known by Spirits all over the world. I would rather allow that character bribe nearby Spirits, avoid Umbra in &quot;middle distance&quot;. All others will not know about that. Also we cannot speak about abusing the Rite as long as there are no cubs among their kids. So even caught red handed she cannot be found guilty. Using this character as NPC another approach can be used: PCs find the remnants of components for this Rite. But who used it? On who? And why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T14:55:08-08:00","id":1424360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424353#post1424353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Why are you all so obessed with killing? Remember, Metis or not, he's still a Garou. And not all old and disabled are eliminated. I remember an NPC from &quot;Caerns: Places of Power&quot;, from Get of Fenris Schwartzwald caern, who was attacked and horribly deformed by Tzimisce and yet they allow her to live. In one of the harshest caerns in the world. You are also right about Garou being a dying race. That's why more and more Metis are allowed to live. Their parents too. And that's why I also had a Ragabash NPC who, inspired by Sabbat Mass Embraces, stated that every Garou, regardless of race, should bring at least one Metis to this world (to buy Gaia some time), mate with a wolf (with more children from one pregnancy chances for Garou are bigger) then move to mate with his proper race. Besides I know that every two Garou union ends with a Metis child. I rather try to find a relatively easy way to avoid that. Easy enough to be worth a try, hard enough to be an exception and not destroy the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That metis was accepted and respected for not taking the easy option, instead living up to the tribe's belief in taking hardship and surviving it. That respect is not something given to every metis.<br /> <br /> We are obsessed with killing, because the Garou Nation is extremely likely to kill those who do not toe the line. The fact that metis are allowed to live more often is seen as a BAD thing for more traditionalist tribes. Something tolerated ONLY due to not having any other option. It is not a good thing, but it is part of the setting.<br /> <br /> As for intentional metis creation, garou cannot risk 10 years and a loss of a warrior for a hope of decent shock troops. Even BSDs don't rely on that method. It is just more waste than it is worth.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T15:08:49-08:00","id":1424365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424360#post1424360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That metis was accepted and respected for not taking the easy option, instead living up to the tribe's belief in taking hardship and surviving it. That respect is not something given to every metis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. But I mentioned her as an example. Even in core rulebooks you can find informations that more often than not Metis are allowed to live.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424360#post1424360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We are obsessed with killing, because the Garou Nation is extremely likely to kill those who do not toe the line. The fact that metis are allowed to live more often is seen as a BAD thing for more traditionalist tribes. Something tolerated ONLY due to not having any other option. It is not a good thing, but it is part of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it is. But it's also the easy way. Kill everyone, Gaia will recognize her own. I prefere the more vampire-esque approach: &quot;the monster I am lest the monster I become&quot;. How far you can go. How fanatically will you fight for your beliefs. And how much can you sacrifice for that. Maybe that's why, during my games, a lot of player characters end as Ronin or in Harano. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424360#post1424360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for intentional metis creation, garou cannot risk 10 years and a loss of a warrior for a hope of decent shock troops. Even BSDs don't rely on that method. It is just more waste than it is worth.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say that this theory is right or wrong, stupid or wise. Only that there is one. But the look on my player's/PC's faces is priceless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T01:16:31-08:00","id":1424481,"title":"","content":"About Summer Country:<br /> Metis are cured TEMPORARY, and if they leave the Realm, they revert. If you stay too long, you may disconnect. Entering the Summer Country requires the Garou to be peace with Gaia (himself, environment, every living beeing). Two Garou who don't accept their rule / place are not acceptable to enter the SC.<br /> <br /> Rites: I see one type of spirit who would be veeery happy to jump into the line. Banes. But still, the spirit world shall not accept this usage of the punishment rite as it goes against the roles of spirits &amp; Garou.<br /> Other: Can you steel what is not-existing? The pre-first change Garou doesn't posess rage.<br /> I see that you'd still allow this NPC. Of course, you created it. But I still advise to see in a broader spectrum and notice, how much she is not fitting.<br /> <br /> Note: There are easily accessible medications (check Maggadon products) which can supress the first change. I'd accept if those stuff would be used, but using rites a way what shall not work is bad.<br /> Add: For the rites, except minor &amp; mystical 3 Garous are needed. Who were the other two?<br /> <br /> About the Ragabash: The birth of a metis could hurt / maim / kill the mother. The metis is not able to give birth. This goes against to every &quot;mass-creation&quot; goal. Breeding with wolves is the matemathically acceptable solution.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I've found a possible way to have a baby &quot;almost together&quot;. In Vitro Fertilisation. Sperm of the male Garou, egg of a Kinfolk. It should work, except if there is some unforseeable stuff with the homeobox genes of female Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":562,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","user":"Lachdanan","date":". 11-17-2020, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T01:36:40-08:00","id":1424487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424365#post1424365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course it is. But it's also the easy way. Kill everyone, Gaia will recognize her own. I prefere the more vampire-esque approach: &quot;the monster I am lest the monster I become&quot;. How far you can go. How fanatically will you fight for your beliefs. And how much can you sacrifice for that. Maybe that's why, during my games, a lot of player characters end as Ronin or in Harano.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to tell you how to play WtA, but there is a third sentence for me in that line &quot;The monster I must be.&quot; Unlike Vampire, garou have a VERY clear goal of their existence; Fighting the Wyrm. Everything and anything is done in service of that goal. It is something you cannot ever give up.<br /> <br /> So, in my opinion, even once the garou realise they are utter monsters, there isn't that much they can do about it. Since if they don't act like monsters, the reality as they know it will be corrupted. Even if they hope to make things better once they gain rank, they most likely will die or become jaded before that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T05:37:40-08:00","id":1424524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424326#post1424326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, unless we are talking about BSDs, no canon metis has ever been a wanted child. The common narrative of them, troubling or not, is that their parents fooled around and broke up after the female got pregnant.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Doesn't mean that a wanted child can't happen. Especially, since W20 no has the possibility, that any kinfolk could be a pre-change late bloomer garou. So, two suspected kinfolk could break the Litany now. Great.<br /> <br /> But besides that, the parents rarely have the chance to stay together. They are law breakers and garou society's ways of punishment aren't that numerous. Death, Banishment, Loss of Rank/Renown. But, what Truthcater who deserves his wisdom renown would allow the parents to stay together. They have proven that they were unable to uphold the Litany, how on Gaia would one let them keep living in a situation that is so likely to make them repeat-offenders?<br /> <br /> Well, castration is on the list of Battle Scars, iirc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T07:37:54-08:00","id":1424540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424524#post1424524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But besides that, the parents rarely have the chance to stay together. They are law breakers and garou society's ways of punishment aren't that numerous. Death, Banishment, Loss of Rank/Renown. But, what Truthcater who deserves his wisdom renown would allow the parents to stay together. They have proven that they were unable to uphold the Litany, how on Gaia would one let them keep living in a situation that is so likely to make them repeat-offenders?<br /> <br /> Well, castration is on the list of Battle Scars, iirc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, then we run into the fun argument of whether sex with another garou et al is litany violation or is the creation of a metis the crime XD<br /> <br /> Great for in-game arguments, though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T08:49:23-08:00","id":1424552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424540#post1424540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, then we run into the fun argument of whether sex with another garou et al is litany violation or is the creation of a metis the crime XD<br /> <br /> Great for in-game arguments, though!</div> </div> </div> </div>Or not. We had that argument a couple of times in LARP. Cubs asking the Philodox as well as actual trails of Litany violators.<br /> <br /> It ain't that much fun to go though this, for it is (if no metis is born) a &quot;no harm no foul&quot; situation. At first glance. But, if two years later the sept goes under, because the neighbour sept argues &quot;We won't send packs to help out a bunch on Litany violators and their enablers&quot; the harm is there. And that is, what it basically comes down to. If the PCs are liberal in this matter the ST (or in case of the LARP ST team) has to make to call how the NPC world will react to this behaviour.<br /> <br /> But, besides the implication of the deed itself and what allowing it means and how harsh punishments should be, there is another, more frustrating part to it. The language. Some will argue that &quot;breed&quot; means procreate, so non-child-bearing sex is okay. Other will argue, that &quot;breed&quot; is the closest English word to what intercourse means in the way wolves would express themselves, but that it is the intention to ban all intercourse, for wolves would not communicate with such nuance but get the meaning anyway. Then, one would counter-argue that wolves only mate annually and unlike humans, some monkey specials probably, and dolphins (scientifically proven) actually have fun while having sex and therefore this application is so alien to wolves that this practice can't be included in what they mean when they talk about &quot;breeding&quot;.<br /> And, there is no definitive answer to that argument, since we as players have no real concept of how wolves think. Or how communication works among wolves. And, we don't have the stories from all over the planet that all these millenia ago were brought to Pangea and argued about and from which the tenets of the Litany were condensed. If we knew the source material for the tenet, we could try to try to understand if the tenet came into existence because love between garou always lead to something bad, or if there were other reasons, like the prediction of the metis breed.<br /> All we know, is that the Legend from &quot;Guardians of the Caerns&quot; suggests, that the tenet is older as the first metis and therefore experience with Metis Breed Garou was not the reason the tenet was created - unless time travel.<br /> The assupmtions that garou metis would be bad based on Metis of other Changing Breeds (that were older) might have contributed to the tenet, though. As could have the tenet of other fera Litany, if the garou back then brought these with them to the meeting in Pangea where the Litany was formed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T09:31:27-08:00","id":1424557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424481#post1424481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Summer Country:<br /> Metis are cured TEMPORARY, and if they leave the Realm, they revert. If you stay too long, you may disconnect. Entering the Summer Country requires the Garou to be peace with Gaia (himself, environment, every living beeing). Two Garou who don't accept their rule / place are not acceptable to enter the SC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't recall if it was temporary. In my defence I have to admit that most of sourcebooks I've read were borrowed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424481#post1424481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other: Can you steel what is not-existing? The pre-first change Garou doesn't posess rage.<br /> I see that you'd still allow this NPC. Of course, you created it. But I still advise to see in a broader spectrum and notice, how much she is not fitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Garou before First Change does have Rage. If it hadn't there won't be &quot;mood changes&quot;, &quot;antisocial behaviour&quot; and &quot;strange eeriness&quot;. Plus, quoting one of the characters from &quot;When will you Rage?&quot; (I can't recall his name, I don't have the book right now): &quot;First Change is not the moment we become Garou. It's the realisation of this fact&quot;. And I think that this character can be succesfully used. I saw worse things than that (pack example from &quot;Rite of Passage&quot;, the authors couldn't be less creative; despite this I still found them useful). Besides Garou can be mentally ill, for me that's just one example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424481#post1424481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: There are easily accessible medications (check Maggadon products) which can supress the first change. I'd accept if those stuff would be used, but using rites a way what shall not work is bad.<br /> Add: For the rites, except minor &amp; mystical 3 Garous are needed. Who were the other two?</div> </div> </div> </div>So what if the Rites won't work. She feels that they will. And as I mentioned above she's not perfectly sane. The two other Garou are the smallest problem. They can be their packmates (loyalty to their leader), her first two children (isolated upbringing plus love). Others can be convinced (that's right, my friend, who was a specialist in finding loopholes, once created a greatest speaker in the world; if it's not for the dicecap it would have over 20 dices for Social tests and max difficulty 4), decieved, bribed or intimidated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424481#post1424481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Ragabash: The birth of a metis could hurt / maim / kill the mother. The metis is not able to give birth. This goes against to every &quot;mass-creation&quot; goal. Breeding with wolves is the matemathically acceptable solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally, someone who remember about it. None of my players did (till now, I still use this NPC). Chapeau bas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424481#post1424481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I've found a possible way to have a baby &quot;almost together&quot;. In Vitro Fertilisation. Sperm of the male Garou, egg of a Kinfolk. It should work, except if there is some unforseeable stuff with the homeobox genes of female Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I thought about that too. But it's not what I had in mind. Plus it's too Weaverish for my state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-17-2020, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T09:38:07-08:00","id":1424559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424487#post1424487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not going to tell you how to play WtA, but there is a third sentence for me in that line &amp;quot;The monster I must be.&amp;quot; Unlike Vampire, garou have a VERY clear goal of their existence; Fighting the Wyrm. Everything and anything is done in service of that goal. It is something you cannot ever give up.<br /> <br /> So, in my opinion, even once the garou realise they are utter monsters, there isn't that much they can do about it. Since if they don't act like monsters, the reality as they know it will be corrupted. Even if they hope to make things better once they gain rank, they most likely will die or become jaded before that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't allow you to tell me so \ud83d\ude1c. My rules are simple and one of them says: &quot;if you don't like my style then go find another Storyteller&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for being a monster there are many ways of being one. And not all Garou accept their nature. Most of them (especially homids) have their own problems and they don't need any more of them. That's why the majority of the older ones are jaded, just like you wrote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T09:44:22-08:00","id":1424561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424524#post1424524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. Doesn't mean that a wanted child can't happen. Especially, since W20 no has the possibility, that any kinfolk could be a pre-change late bloomer garou. So, two suspected kinfolk could break the Litany now. Great.<br /> <br /> But besides that, the parents rarely have the chance to stay together. They are law breakers and garou society's ways of punishment aren't that numerous. Death, Banishment, Loss of Rank/Renown. But, what Truthcater who deserves his wisdom renown would allow the parents to stay together. They have proven that they were unable to uphold the Litany, how on Gaia would one let them keep living in a situation that is so likely to make them repeat-offenders?<br /> <br /> Well, castration is on the list of Battle Scars, iirc.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember well from Storyteller's Handbook revised edition Garou before First Change instinctively sense each other (the thing that they loose after it) and will try to avoid the intercourse. That doesn't mean it won't happen of course .This too I used once during my games.<br /> <br /> And castration as a Battle Scar... The punishment which brings you Glory. I like your style. It suits my weird sense of humor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T09:45:18-08:00","id":1424563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424540#post1424540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, then we run into the fun argument of whether sex with another garou et al is litany violation or is the creation of a metis the crime XD<br /> <br /> Great for in-game arguments, though!</div> </div> </div> </div>So my role of Gaillard with a Ragabash sense of humor is fulfilled \ud83d\ude01.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T09:49:48-08:00","id":1424566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1424552#post1424552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or not. We had that argument a couple of times in LARP. Cubs asking the Philodox as well as actual trails of Litany violators.<br /> <br /> It ain't that much fun to go though this, for it is (if no metis is born) a &amp;quot;no harm no foul&amp;quot; situation. At first glance. But, if two years later the sept goes under, because the neighbour sept argues &amp;quot;We won't send packs to help out a bunch on Litany violators and their enablers&amp;quot; the harm is there. And that is, what it basically comes down to. If the PCs are liberal in this matter the ST (or in case of the LARP ST team) has to make to call how the NPC world will react to this behaviour.<br /> <br /> But, besides the implication of the deed itself and what allowing it means and how harsh punishments should be, there is another, more frustrating part to it. The language. Some will argue that &amp;quot;breed&amp;quot; means procreate, so non-child-bearing sex is okay. Other will argue, that &amp;quot;breed&amp;quot; is the closest English word to what intercourse means in the way wolves would express themselves, but that it is the intention to ban all intercourse, for wolves would not communicate with such nuance but get the meaning anyway. Then, one would counter-argue that wolves only mate annually and unlike humans, some monkey specials probably, and dolphins (scientifically proven) actually have fun while having sex and therefore this application is so alien to wolves that this practice can't be included in what they mean when they talk about &amp;quot;breeding&amp;quot;.<br /> And, there is no definitive answer to that argument, since we as players have no real concept of how wolves think. Or how communication works among wolves. And, we don't have the stories from all over the planet that all these millenia ago were brought to Pangea and argued about and from which the tenets of the Litany were condensed. If we knew the source material for the tenet, we could try to try to understand if the tenet came into existence because love between garou always lead to something bad, or if there were other reasons, like the prediction of the metis breed.<br /> All we know, is that the Legend from &amp;quot;Guardians of the Caerns&amp;quot; suggests, that the tenet is older as the first metis and therefore experience with Metis Breed Garou was not the reason the tenet was created - unless time travel.<br /> The assupmtions that garou metis would be bad based on Metis of other Changing Breeds (that were older) might have contributed to the tenet, though. As could have the tenet of other fera Litany, if the garou back then brought these with them to the meeting in Pangea where the Litany was formed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically I agree with that. But there are different tribes and their intepretation of Litany (as it can be seen in Tribebooks) and septs (that goes to the Storyteller). And the arguments and reactions in this topic can be varied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T17:08:43-08:00","id":1425271,"title":"","content":"The Silent Strider Tribebook (Revised) has some things to say about old Garou, losing the wolf, and the Rite of the Winter Wolf.<br /> <br /> Silent Striders don't kill their elders for being old. They don't kill them for losing the wolf. They don't kill them for being sick. They consider killing them if they're incapable of passing down any knowledge (suffering advanced dementia) or suffering constant physical pain that cannot be treated. Otherwise, they treasure their elders because once they die, their spirits are gone forever. No Ancestors background. No summonable ancestor spirits. No path to reach the Tribal Homeland. The Striders don't even know if they <i>have</i> immortal souls like other Garou.<br /> <br /> Second, Silent Striders has an example of a very old Strider elder who lost the wolf and lived like a Kinfolk for many years. At the age of like 104 he got in a fight, got his Rage back, and died in combat in Crinos form. Which demonstrates:<br /> <br /> 1. Garou are Garou from birth to death and losing their Rage doesn't change a thing.<br /> 2. Killing your elders because they're &quot;useless&quot; is exceptionally dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T09:20:50-08:00","id":1425366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425271#post1425271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Silent Strider Tribebook (Revised) has some things to say about old Garou, losing the wolf, and the Rite of the Winter Wolf.<br /> <br /> Silent Striders don't kill their elders for being old. They don't kill them for losing the wolf. They don't kill them for being sick. They consider killing them if they're incapable of passing down any knowledge (suffering advanced dementia) or suffering constant physical pain that cannot be treated. Otherwise, they treasure their elders because once they die, their spirits are gone forever. No Ancestors background. No summonable ancestor spirits. No path to reach the Tribal Homeland. The Striders don't even know if they <i>have</i> immortal souls like other Garou.<br /> <br /> Second, Silent Striders has an example of a very old Strider elder who lost the wolf and lived like a Kinfolk for many years. At the age of like 104 he got in a fight, got his Rage back, and died in combat in Crinos form. Which demonstrates:<br /> <br /> 1. Garou are Garou from birth to death and losing their Rage doesn't change a thing.<br /> 2. Killing your elders because they're &amp;quot;useless&amp;quot; is exceptionally dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. That's what I've been talking about. As for Garou losing the wolf it's true that they are still Garou. BUT there are as many viewpoints as there are Garou (OK, maybe less, not all of them are from Poland \ud83d\ude1c) so there is a chance that there are some who consider themselves Kinfolks when they become rageless (they are not &quot;complete&quot;) and some who view them as Kinfolks (causes they are no match for a &quot;normal&quot; Garou). Besides losing the wolf isn't only losing the ability to shapeshift but also losing many gifts, ability to regenerate (if only partially), moving faster etc. So they are not so different from an ordinary Kinfolk. And that's what I was talking about, not about the viewpotint of an entire society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T09:56:57-08:00","id":1425369,"title":"","content":"Oh right, many might regard them as no longer &quot;true&quot; Garou, although most Tribes generally respect their elders! But I was mentioning it specifically in the context of breeding.<br /> <br /> I still wonder how horny, teenage cubs who haven't changed yet avoid inbreeding. I'd expect this to be a recurring problem, with frequent mules being born... but it doesn't come up in the books I have. I don't recall any Garou railing against teenage promiscuity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T10:09:32-08:00","id":1425370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425369#post1425369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh right, many might regard them as no longer &quot;true&quot; Garou, although most Tribes generally respect their elders! But I was mentioning it specifically in the context of breeding.<br /> <br /> I still wonder how horny, teenage cubs who haven't changed yet avoid inbreeding. I'd expect this to be a recurring problem, with frequent mules being born... but it doesn't come up in the books I have. I don't recall any Garou railing against teenage promiscuity.</div> </div> </div> </div>In one of the Storyteller's Handbook (I believe it was the revised one) it was said that they instinctively sense each other (I mentioned that in one of my earlier posts) and avoid the intercourse. Besides the chances for a meeting of two cubs before First Change aren't so big. But that doesn't mean that ever happens (I use that in one of my stories). And there is also GHB if you want to use some drastic methods. That's why I always ask my players how dark my World of Darkness should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-21-2020, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T10:27:19-08:00","id":1425373,"title":"","content":"What is GHB?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T10:53:28-08:00","id":1425378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425373#post1425373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is GHB?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamma-Hydroxybutyric_acid\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9f/GHB-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamma-Hydroxybutyric_acid\" target=\"_blank\"> &gamma;-Hydroxybutyric acid - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamma-Hydroxybutyric_acid\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamma-Hydroxybutyric_acid </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Very nasty substance .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T14:48:21-08:00","id":1425563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425369#post1425369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still wonder how horny, teenage cubs who haven't changed yet avoid inbreeding. I'd expect this to be a recurring problem, with frequent mules being born... but it doesn't come up in the books I have. I don't recall any Garou railing against teenage promiscuity.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are lots of things one must simply determine on their own for the setting because it's not directly relevant to the actions of most RPG games, so they never get mentioned. It is also going to be something different STs and gaming groups will determine on their own based on their own group's ideas and needs. I think it's best the game does not down into that detail so everyone can come up with something they feel works best, and they don't have to worry about that they are violating canon.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, of course I have my own ideas. Garou culture, on the whole, is very traditional. They are not creatures of modernity and do not hold modern values. Yet their kinfolk in many parts of the world live in modern societies and their culture is being undermined by modern values.<br /> <br /> I imagine most tribes promote cultural values for their kinfolk that would seem antiquated, quaint, backward, or even oppressive to much of the game's fanbase (and therefore, it is frequently ignored). They don't like promiscuity; want strong, stable marriages for life; and encourage kinfolk to get married as young as possible and raise many children. There are exceptions - the Children of Gaia, Bone Gnawers, and Glass Walkers all have different reasons for adopting more modern views. The CoG are often depicted as free-love hippies, the Glass Walkers deal in an urban environment where their kinfolk are dominated by modern culture, and the Bone Gnawers simply don't care. I imagine the Black Furies are divided - they reject much of modernity, but they dislike traditional cultures more patriarchal mores and want more egalitarian conditions if not outright female leadership (though perhaps in informal or secret conspiracies that can't be seen by outsiders).<br /> <br /> As for the possibility for pre-Change Garou accidentally mating with each other, I imagine this is something monitored for by Garou who &quot;oversee&quot; these closed kinfolk communities. To a certain degree, this is policed by the Rite of Baptism by Fire, the Gift Scent of True form in previous editions, and close inspection by the Garou over their kinfolk charges looking for obvious signs that someone may be approaching their first change. Since most Garou are supposed to change sometime during adolescence, this likely stops being an issue when kinfolk reach the age of consent/maturity anyway.<br /> <br /> I think how serious an effort is made depends a lot on the specifics of that kinfolk community. Isolated communities near caerns are probably very strict about such things. Kinfolk who are integrated with normal humans and under more of a modern cultural influence, this becomes progressively harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T16:12:29-08:00","id":1425576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425563#post1425563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As for the possibility for pre-Change Garou accidentally mating with each other, I imagine this is something monitored for by Garou who &quot;oversee&quot; these closed kinfolk communities. To a certain degree, this is policed by the Rite of Baptism by Fire, the Gift Scent of True form in previous editions, and close inspection by the Garou over their kinfolk charges looking for obvious signs that someone may be approaching their first change. Since most Garou are supposed to change sometime during adolescence, this likely stops being an issue when kinfolk reach the age of consent/maturity anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, we are not talking about teenagers between 15-19. We are talking about them being around 11-19, with most garou changing 'round 12-14.<br /> <br /> So its simply avoided by most of the potential garou being just plain kids. Kids that have parents watching over them VEEERY strictly in most tribes.<br /> <br /> With lost cubs, even then the chances are extremely minimal, since they'd be more concerned about being a monster than anything else.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T00:04:32-08:00","id":1425668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425563#post1425563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are lots of things one must simply determine on their own for the setting because it's not directly relevant to the actions of most RPG games, so they never get mentioned. It is also going to be something different STs and gaming groups will determine on their own based on their own group's ideas and needs. I think it's best the game does not down into that detail so everyone can come up with something they feel works best, and they don't have to worry about that they are violating canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>On one hand you are correct. On the other I believe that there should be some canon (the more detailed the better) to allow different STs &quot;exchange&quot; the characters and players. For example I run a story for cubs (after First Change, but before Rite of Passage) and one of the players said that he wants to play his old character, IV Generation 800 years old Malkavian (yes, the one I've mentioned before) and he was very upset I didn't allow that. He said that he played this character for a few years, his old ST let him do it and he didn't understand that I didn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425563#post1425563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nevertheless, of course I have my own ideas. Garou culture, on the whole, is very traditional. They are not creatures of modernity and do not hold modern values. Yet their kinfolk in many parts of the world live in modern societies and their culture is being undermined by modern values.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that in most places this traditional culture faded away. Many caerns can be freely visited by mortals (Sept of the Green, that one from Vancouver in a restaurant, Western Eye sept), many Garou and Kinfolks adopting more modern way of life (I remember a short story from old Storyteller's Handbook about ex Ahroun Wendigo who was seduced by city and became Grass Walker Theurge). They would like to see the return of the old ways but now it's impossible. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425563#post1425563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine most tribes promote cultural values for their kinfolk that would seem antiquated, quaint, backward, or even oppressive to much of the game's fanbase (and therefore, it is frequently ignored). They don't like promiscuity; want strong, stable marriages for life; and encourage kinfolk to get married as young as possible and raise many children. There are exceptions - the Children of Gaia, Bone Gnawers, and Glass Walkers all have different reasons for adopting more modern views. The CoG are often depicted as free-love hippies, the Glass Walkers deal in an urban environment where their kinfolk are dominated by modern culture, and the Bone Gnawers simply don't care. I imagine the Black Furies are divided - they reject much of modernity, but they dislike traditional cultures more patriarchal mores and want more egalitarian conditions if not outright female leadership (though perhaps in informal or secret conspiracies that can't be seen by outsiders).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I noticed that too. Many players don't understand that society and ignore it. On the other hand most people aren't good actors (including myself) so they aren't good players. They are adequate at best. But, as I think that Garou society changed, there's hope for them \ud83d\ude1c. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425563#post1425563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the possibility for pre-Change Garou accidentally mating with each other, I imagine this is something monitored for by Garou who &amp;quot;oversee&amp;quot; these closed kinfolk communities. To a certain degree, this is policed by the Rite of Baptism by Fire, the Gift Scent of True form in previous editions, and close inspection by the Garou over their kinfolk charges looking for obvious signs that someone may be approaching their first change. Since most Garou are supposed to change sometime during adolescence, this likely stops being an issue when kinfolk reach the age of consent/maturity anyway.<br /> <br /> I think how serious an effort is made depends a lot on the specifics of that kinfolk community. Isolated communities near caerns are probably very strict about such things. Kinfolk who are integrated with normal humans and under more of a modern cultural influence, this becomes progressively harder.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, if we think about closed communities. But in modern world, where one can travel to the other side of the world in just few hours it is nearly impossible to track every Kinfolk. Plus ignoring all those who hadn't changed early in their life is a straight way to end with a Metis (even if it's not so common).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T00:26:27-08:00","id":1425671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425576#post1425576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, we are not talking about teenagers between 15-19. We are talking about them being around 11-19, with most garou changing 'round 12-14.<br /> <br /> So its simply avoided by most of the potential garou being just plain kids. Kids that have parents watching over them VEEERY strictly in most tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoretically yes. But on the other hand I saw every template from every sourcebook and, assuming that their First Change happened one year before their &quot;final version&quot;, at least 10 of them are 20+ when they first shapeshift (based of their bio or/and picture), at least one more of the rest is sexually active (condoms mentioned in the equipment) and at least two of them have kids. Many of them are from dysfunctional families. And if we assume that if they don't have Kinfolk Background their families don't know about Garou and analyze their bios most of them were under the Septs radar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425576#post1425576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With lost cubs, even then the chances are extremely minimal, since they'd be more concerned about being a monster than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the chances for 2 Lost Cubs meeting each other and starting the intercourse are slim at best. I think that's even less possible than one of the &quot;official&quot; cubs mating with the lost one. And of course we cannot assume that only cubs can end with an unplanned Metis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T06:03:46-08:00","id":1425713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425671#post1425671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Theoretically yes. But on the other hand I saw every template from every sourcebook and, assuming that their First Change happened one year before their &quot;final version&quot;, at least 10 of them are 20+ when they first shapeshift (based of their bio or/and picture), at least one more of the rest is sexually active (condoms mentioned in the equipment) and at least two of them have kids. Many of them are from dysfunctional families. And if we assume that if they don't have Kinfolk Background their families don't know about Garou and analyze their bios most of them were under the Septs radar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Templates tend to be rather hit and miss, revised OR 2nd ed. As much I'd WANT to say they are accurate, we have a librarian lupus dr.House the Wendigo, the wyrm-tainted Fenrir metis ahroun template for Get of Fenris revised and other such things. Besides, when it comes to setting accuracy, a lot of non-signature NPCs have human jobs (or are an ahroun hockey player.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T11:26:19-08:00","id":1425768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425713#post1425713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Templates tend to be rather hit and miss, revised OR 2nd ed. As much I'd WANT to say they are accurate, we have a librarian lupus dr.House the Wendigo, the wyrm-tainted Fenrir metis ahroun template for Get of Fenris revised and other such things. Besides, when it comes to setting accuracy, a lot of non-signature NPCs have human jobs (or are an ahroun hockey player.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that they are all good (but I had to admit that I like that hockey player and I can understand that metis Get). I also think that if we play &quot;by the book&quot; most characters will be unplayable because of family and friends. If I imagine myself and my friends, who were my first W:tA players back in the 90's, as a pack of teenagers only one of us had parents who wouldn't mind him fight the Wyrm. The same with a pack example from &quot;Rite of Passage&quot;: Lupus Ahroun Get of Fenris doesn't have close family, the same with Metis Theurge Uktena and Homid Gaillard Shadow Lord comes from a dysfunctional family. The rest, Philodox of Children of Gaia and Ragabash Glass Walker both Homids, would have their families on their back (and none of them Kinfolks). Judging by pictures they aren't more then 17 years old. The second thing: I believe that most of the 12-14 years old, after being told who are they, would rather react &quot;GREAT!!! Beware bullies&quot; then &quot;GREAT!!! Now I will lead a glorious life of one of Gaia's chosen one&quot;. And the last one thing: as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> wrote most Garou communities promote values that are at least outdated. Long time ago there were many cultures who would see 12-14 years old as ready for marriage and pregnancy. Even today there are some of them (some of them are even new) which think that if a boy/girl is prolific then they are ready for mating. And, if assumed that Garou are beings driving by instinct, they would too see a young teenager as ready for mating, not as kids (look at the wolves, 2 years old so as lupus right after First Change =12-14 years old Homid). The rest is the influence of a human society. I belive that's why on most pictures ready-to-play characters are at least 18-20 years old. The authors saw what they wrote earlier and decided that's wrong. What we do in private during our games could be seen as criminally offensive if put into the officially published books (even the Black Dog ones).<br /> <br /> EDIT: there were 2 Garou hockey players (both playing for Oilers), one only mentioned in the description of the Wendigo. The second one was a Silver Fang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-23-2020, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T17:12:46-08:00","id":1425812,"title":"","content":"The game's setting described in the corebook assumes most Garou change around adolescence. They are either raised in knowing kinfolk families to have Garou values, or are runaways from their lost kinfolk/human parents. In either case, normal humans would ostracize them to various degrees because of the Curse. Their &quot;job&quot; for the most part is simply being Garou. After several years of tutelage as cubs, Garou begin their advance as rank in their late teens.<br /> <br /> I will have to admit I have never seen a group of PCs fit this description (there have been individual exceptions within a group that mainly does not fit). Furthermore, most NPCs in games I've played in also do not fit this description. Even cubs - PCs or NPCs - are late teens at their youngest.<br /> <br /> Instead I see many late changing Garou who already have careers - often successful ones, and they continue in those careers as Garou. I think there are several reasons for that.<br /> <br /> First, the time scale of many chronicles don't really allow aging so any PCs are essentially &quot;trapped&quot; in that age forever. While I know many players who don't mind starting in their teens, are running preludes of that age, they perceive their character in at least young adult terms - mid twenties to early thirties. They don't want to play characters who couldn't even legally get into a bar - at least not for the entire game. And most chronicles take place &quot;now&quot; and don't allow for the passage of time. Second, players in general love to frontload accomplishments and achievements into their character background. And a character needs time to do that. You have to at least be in your early to mid-twenties to be combat veterans, professionals like lawyers, successful businessmen, etc. That can't be done if your PC starts at age 16. Third, people really see &quot;career/job&quot; as a defining characteristic - so their character concepts often start with that. They want certain skills, life events, and training that is unlikely to have happened to adolescents. Fourth, they want to interact with the human world and don't want to do so as scary, unemployed vagabonds who'd have the cops called on them constantly.<br /> <br /> I don't see this in fantasy RPG settings, but this is how it goes in any setting that takes place in the modern real world or sci-fi equivalent. And most of the other WoD game lines support this because being turned into a vampire, awakening into a mage, or dying can happen at later dates. Changeling has a similar problem as Werewolf - every PC is at least a late Wilder or a Grump. I've never seen someone play a Childing, or really use those as NPCs.<br /> <br /> So I think there is often a tension between the game's setting as written in the corebook, and how people actually run games. And Werewolf character templates usually reflect that. They don't reflect the setting as described in the corebook. They describe it by how people usually play it - which ignores a lot of supposedly key features of the setting.<br /> <br /> When I ST games, I don't even try to police this with the players although I do encourage them to start as young as possible. Instead, I work on making the NPCs reflect the setting accurately, and usually run games in the recent past (anywhere from starting several decades ago to a century ago) so we can have the passage of time during the game and try to have the game take place over several years if not several decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T17:59:54-08:00","id":1425818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425812#post1425812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game's setting described in the corebook assumes most Garou change around adolescence. They are either raised in knowing kinfolk families to have Garou values, or are runaways from their lost kinfolk/human parents. In either case, normal humans would ostracize them to various degrees because of the Curse. Their &quot;job&quot; for the most part is simply being Garou. After several years of tutelage as cubs, Garou begin their advance as rank in their late teens.<br /> <br /> I will have to admit I have never seen a group of PCs fit this description (there have been individual exceptions within a group that mainly does not fit). Furthermore, most NPCs in games I've played in also do not fit this description. Even cubs - PCs or NPCs - are late teens at their youngest.<br /> <br /> Instead I see many late changing Garou who already have careers - often successful ones, and they continue in those careers as Garou. I think there are several reasons for that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It IS interesting how much in conflict the templates of official books are to the actual rules. I don't mean it as a bad thing, I just mean its weird that they didn't go around and change things over the editions to reflect the templates/NPCs better.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the idea of them starting young and not having much human connection outside kinfolk. Thus making having kinfolk such a HUGE need. Plus it fits with lupus and metis shift ages. I know I'm in the minority on this, but it makes the isolation from humanity that much more meaningful.<br /> <br /> If you could just continue being a succesful tech mogul as an ahroun shadow lord, it would take away from the need for kin AND the feeling of being forever removed from those you grew up with.<br /> <br /> But this is just my take, and I'm fine with others'.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T00:22:30-08:00","id":1425871,"title":"","content":"I also think, that for a lot of the templates in the TBs the normal background of the game doesn't make so much sense.<br /> <br /> When Black Fox writes, that garou are &quot;cubs&quot; for several years, where they get training, I wonder if there is a reference for that. Because, I vaguely remember some garou being thrown into their &quot;Rite of Passage&quot; pretty fast, but I'm not sure if these were from the books or from the LARP, back when I joined the game 20 years ago (man, I'm old).<br /> <br /> Pre-W20, when one could be certain if a person was a garou or a kinfolk, even pre-change, there was certainly potential for a two class upbringing of children within the kinfolk community. One out of eight (factoring in Pure Breed and talens to help with breeding true) would be a chosen warrior and certainly raised another way than their kinfolk siblings/cousins/peers. With the Curse already present, they also would need special consideration regarding their education. Public school would be difficult, but home schooling isn't an option every where. In Germany for example, school is mandatory and exceptions are rare. The number of garou wouldn't be so high as to get permits for private schools (which also may be suspicious once hunter figure that out). A boarding school might be an option, but all septs in Germany would hardly fill one school, unless kinfolk was also permitted, and even then the different tribes might object sending their kids there.<br /> <br /> Post-W20, one can't be sure if a kid is garou or not, and that leads to whole new dynamic. Does one educate all kids in a way that prepares them to be garou, or none? Starting from what age would one try to see if there are indicators of the Curse when interacting with humans? How accurate can this be?<br /> <br /> &quot;Warriors of the Apocalypse&quot; has backgrounds to some characters from the WtA-based TCG. I always liked the story of &quot;Anna something&quot;, who was raised as a garou and part-took in garou festivities even pre-change. When during a Rite emotions ran high, she had her First Change and entered a frenzy. A (supposed) loss of Renown for which her father disowned her on the spot, and she challenged him for that. Having been trained by her father and being basically inexperienced she shouldn't have had a chance, but she had mastered a combat move from another teacher her father didn't expect and she bested and killed him. Claiming his Klaive she also proclaimed Cliath rank for herself, and the sept agreed.<br /> I didn't re-read the story, it's the way I remember it. This is a very bad-ass story, but it wouldn't make sense under W20 rules, for a kid wouldn't be trained like a garou.<br /> <br /> In our LARP palyers are all older than 20 and even those who join for the first time play as cubs when they start. So, we ignore the whole &quot;first change in adolescence&quot; and the danger of becoming a Lunatic for the most part. Still, we try to make players aware, that their characters probably aren't the most successful entrepreneurs or have any career where interaction with people is required, due to the Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T01:07:34-08:00","id":1425875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425812#post1425812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game's setting described in the corebook assumes most Garou change around adolescence. They are either raised in knowing kinfolk families to have Garou values, or are runaways from their lost kinfolk/human parents. In either case, normal humans would ostracize them to various degrees because of the Curse. Their &quot;job&quot; for the most part is simply being Garou. After several years of tutelage as cubs, Garou begin their advance as rank in their late teens.<br /> <br /> I will have to admit I have never seen a group of PCs fit this description (there have been individual exceptions within a group that mainly does not fit). Furthermore, most NPCs in games I've played in also do not fit this description. Even cubs - PCs or NPCs - are late teens at their youngest.<br /> <br /> Instead I see many late changing Garou who already have careers - often successful ones, and they continue in those careers as Garou. I think there are several reasons for that.<br /> <br /> First, the time scale of many chronicles don't really allow aging so any PCs are essentially &quot;trapped&quot; in that age forever. While I know many players who don't mind starting in their teens, are running preludes of that age, they perceive their character in at least young adult terms - mid twenties to early thirties. They don't want to play characters who couldn't even legally get into a bar - at least not for the entire game. And most chronicles take place &quot;now&quot; and don't allow for the passage of time. Second, players in general love to frontload accomplishments and achievements into their character background. And a character needs time to do that. You have to at least be in your early to mid-twenties to be combat veterans, professionals like lawyers, successful businessmen, etc. That can't be done if your PC starts at age 16. Third, people really see &quot;career/job&quot; as a defining characteristic - so their character concepts often start with that. They want certain skills, life events, and training that is unlikely to have happened to adolescents. Fourth, they want to interact with the human world and don't want to do so as scary, unemployed vagabonds who'd have the cops called on them constantly.<br /> <br /> I don't see this in fantasy RPG settings, but this is how it goes in any setting that takes place in the modern real world or sci-fi equivalent. And most of the other WoD game lines support this because being turned into a vampire, awakening into a mage, or dying can happen at later dates. Changeling has a similar problem as Werewolf - every PC is at least a late Wilder or a Grump. I've never seen someone play a Childing, or really use those as NPCs.<br /> <br /> So I think there is often a tension between the game's setting as written in the corebook, and how people actually run games. And Werewolf character templates usually reflect that. They don't reflect the setting as described in the corebook. They describe it by how people usually play it - which ignores a lot of supposedly key features of the setting.<br /> <br /> When I ST games, I don't even try to police this with the players although I do encourage them to start as young as possible. Instead, I work on making the NPCs reflect the setting accurately, and usually run games in the recent past (anywhere from starting several decades ago to a century ago) so we can have the passage of time during the game and try to have the game take place over several years if not several decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I've been talking about. Playing &quot;by the rules&quot; is nearly impossible. Especially that I don't agree with you that training lasts for several years. I think it's more a year or so. Especially if the cub was raised by Kinfolks, they wouldn't mind the sept talking them over after the First Change. With cubs raised by ordinary mortals that would be a bigger problem. Funny thing, most ready-to-play characters doesn't have Kinfolk Background and don't mention them in their bios. As for templates are I remember only one who seemed to be about 12 years old, a Wendigo Ragabash from 2nd edition Tribebook.<br /> <br /> As for players I've been experimenting with various methods of creating the characters. The one I use now divides the responsibilities of creating them between my players who describes background and me rulling the dots. It goes like that: players decide their characters DoB, fills some things like medical and school chart, police rap sheet (if there are any) and, with that as a base I fill the character sheet like that: <br /> <br /> Attributes 7/5/3 (Garou are homo sapiens superior; they have a headstart if we consider the attributes; the only exception is Appereance cause I know players who won't accept characters with Appereance below 3).<br /> Abilities 11/7/4 (they are ordinary teenagers, the rest they will get after the training; I allow them to decide). Restricted abilities are Streetwise, Drive, Firearms, Melee, Bureaucracy and Medicine, unless the character's background justifies that. Max 2 dots on every trait, unless the charater is planned as a professional in one area.<br /> Backgrounds varies (generally my decision, especially Pure Breed, Ancestors and Fetish, I also use backgrounds system from 1st Edition, with dots restrictions based on Tribes).<br /> Freebies 18 (distributed according to bios).<br /> <br /> Auspice is based on DoB (plus potential planetary Merits&amp;Flaws), they are members of the tribe which got them first. <br /> <br /> That way the players &quot;get&quot; (they don't have access to their character sheets) an untrained base but with a lot of Backgrounds and secondary abilities (usually). That makes their lives harder but, on the other hand, more realistic. As for advancing in age and experience I wrote about that in other thread.<br /> <br /> You could also notice that there are didn't mention Metis (the same &quot;rules&quot;, but as they usually live near the sept their skills will rather be useful in fighting the Wyrm, more like John Connor's in Terminator) and lupus (I rarely allow playing lupus but if I do I use standard lupus rules). My players accepted that and we have fun playing (there were no complaints, on the other hand no one forces them to play with me). I run the Preludes of course, to faciliate filling the dots.<br /> <br /> I also don't have a problem with character's aging. My stories rarely have a clear start and finish so there are only two ways to end: death or player's decision that he/she has enough and puts the character away.<br /> <br /> I also plan to start a LARP. The character creation will be basically the same, except for those who wants to play more advanced characters. In that case they will get 3 sets of question, one set for Race, Auspice and Tribe they want to play, one question for each rank (the higher rank, the tougher questions, not always from W:tA sourcebooks). That way I will decide their ranks and add some freebies accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-24-2020, 04:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T01:33:48-08:00","id":1425876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425818#post1425818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I like the idea of them starting young and not having much human connection outside kinfolk. Thus making having kinfolk such a HUGE need. Plus it fits with lupus and metis shift ages. I know I'm in the minority on this, but it makes the isolation from humanity that much more meaningful.<br /> <br /> If you could just continue being a succesful tech mogul as an ahroun shadow lord, it would take away from the need for kin AND the feeling of being forever removed from those you grew up with.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the Preludes are for. And I don't think the isolation and being raised by Kinfolks is the only was to achive that. Losing a mortal family or friend hurts the same (I know what I'm talking about, I buried both of them and Garou are more sensitive creatures with Rage boiling in them).<br /> <br /> As for Kinfolks, taking my rather big family as an example, I prefere Allies over Kinfolks. They are close enough to the character to hurt them if they heel turn, yet they should be kept in the dark about character's nature. And usually their capabilities are bigger. Back to the example: my family (Kinfolks) could help me (a Garou) as driver, translator, lend me some money, patch me after a fight or give a place to crash. Among my close friends (Allies) and colleagues (Contacts) are lawyer, two of them work at City Hall, a rock singer, a TV journalist, I also know a high placed guy in one of the video games companies. So who could hurt me more if given the reason?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-24-2020, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T01:50:59-08:00","id":1425878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425876#post1425876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's the Preludes are for. And I don't think the isolation and being raised by Kinfolks is the only was to achive that. Losing a mortal family or friend hurts the same (I know what I'm talking about, I buried both of them and Garou are more sensitive creatures with Rage boiling in them).<br /> <br /> As for Kinfolks, taking my rather big family as an example, I prefere Allies over Kinfolks. They are close enough to the character to hurt them if they heel turn, yet they should be kept in the dark about character's nature. And usually their capabilities are bigger. Back to the example: my family (Kinfolks) could help me (a Garou) as driver, translator, lend me some money, patch me after a fight or give a place to crash. Among my close friends (Allies) and colleagues (Contacts) are lawyer, two of them work at City Hall, a rock singer, a TV journalist, I also know a high placed guy in one of the video games companies. So who could hurt me more if given the reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, I don't mean isolation as in being raised with kinfolk, I mean the isolation of being scary to 30-90% of humans and being unable to hold a regular job.<br /> <br /> That's the thing with kinfolk, they are the bridge between garou and humans. They don't have Rage, but they can have powers.<br /> <br /> Yet, despite WtA being 20+ years old, we still run into this &quot;garou template/npc is a succesful in a field that requires 50% of their time&quot; issue. Which then is impossible by the stats. So, why has it not been changed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T01:59:17-08:00","id":1425880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425871#post1425871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think, that for a lot of the templates in the TBs the normal background of the game doesn't make so much sense.<br /> <br /> When Black Fox writes, that garou are &amp;quot;cubs&amp;quot; for several years, where they get training, I wonder if there is a reference for that. Because, I vaguely remember some garou being thrown into their &amp;quot;Rite of Passage&amp;quot; pretty fast, but I'm not sure if these were from the books or from the LARP, back when I joined the game 20 years ago (man, I'm old).<br /> <br /> Pre-W20, when one could be certain if a person was a garou or a kinfolk, even pre-change, there was certainly potential for a two class upbringing of children within the kinfolk community. One out of eight (factoring in Pure Breed and talens to help with breeding true) would be a chosen warrior and certainly raised another way than their kinfolk siblings/cousins/peers. With the Curse already present, they also would need special consideration regarding their education. Public school would be difficult, but home schooling isn't an option every where. In Germany for example, school is mandatory and exceptions are rare. The number of garou wouldn't be so high as to get permits for private schools (which also may be suspicious once hunter figure that out). A boarding school might be an option, but all septs in Germany would hardly fill one school, unless kinfolk was also permitted, and even then the different tribes might object sending their kids there.<br /> <br /> Post-W20, one can't be sure if a kid is garou or not, and that leads to whole new dynamic. Does one educate all kids in a way that prepares them to be garou, or none? Starting from what age would one try to see if there are indicators of the Curse when interacting with humans? How accurate can this be?<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Warriors of the Apocalypse&amp;quot; has backgrounds to some characters from the WtA-based TCG. I always liked the story of &amp;quot;Anna something&amp;quot;, who was raised as a garou and part-took in garou festivities even pre-change. When during a Rite emotions ran high, she had her First Change and entered a frenzy. A (supposed) loss of Renown for which her father disowned her on the spot, and she challenged him for that. Having been trained by her father and being basically inexperienced she shouldn't have had a chance, but she had mastered a combat move from another teacher her father didn't expect and she bested and killed him. Claiming his Klaive she also proclaimed Cliath rank for herself, and the sept agreed.<br /> I didn't re-read the story, it's the way I remember it. This is a very bad-ass story, but it wouldn't make sense under W20 rules, for a kid wouldn't be trained like a garou.<br /> <br /> In our LARP palyers are all older than 20 and even those who join for the first time play as cubs when they start. So, we ignore the whole &amp;quot;first change in adolescence&amp;quot; and the danger of becoming a Lunatic for the most part. Still, we try to make players aware, that their characters probably aren't the most successful entrepreneurs or have any career where interaction with people is required, due to the Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I remember there wasn't any rules of training the Cubs (nor there was any timeframe). I believe that the best description of training was written in various Tribebooks (I like Fianna the most) where the entire story of a Tribe, Litany and a few words about other Tribes were told. I think that remembering that (in your one words, not literally, The Litany being the only exception) shouldn't take more than a month. The rest is learning the Gifts and Rituals, entering the Umbra, activate Talens and Fetishes, using Rage, shapeshifting, combat etc. That's why I assumed that it shouldn't take more than a year. Rite of Passage is another story. In most cases the Cub can &quot;replay&quot; the Rite as long as there will be one of two endings: success or death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T02:01:40-08:00","id":1425881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425878#post1425878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh no, I don't mean isolation as in being raised with kinfolk, I mean the isolation of being scary to 30-90% of humans and being unable to hold a regular job.<br /> <br /> That's the thing with kinfolk, they are the bridge between garou and humans. They don't have Rage, but they can have powers.<br /> <br /> Yet, despite WtA being 20+ years old, we still run into this &amp;quot;garou template/npc is a succesful in a field that requires 50% of their time&amp;quot; issue. Which then is impossible by the stats. So, why has it not been changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I missunderstood you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T02:56:18-08:00","id":1425889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425880#post1425880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I remember there wasn't any rules of training the Cubs (nor there was any timeframe). I believe that the best description of training was written in various Tribebooks (I like Fianna the most) where the entire story of a Tribe, Litany and a few words about other Tribes were told. I think that remembering that (in your one words, not literally, The Litany being the only exception) shouldn't take more than a month. The rest is learning the Gifts and Rituals, entering the Umbra, activate Talens and Fetishes, using Rage, shapeshifting, combat etc. That's why I assumed that it shouldn't take more than a year. Rite of Passage is another story. In most cases the Cub can &quot;replay&quot; the Rite as long as there will be one of two endings: success or death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, too, would guess that a year of being a cub is a good assumption. Some might need more time, others less, but when they hit 20 years of age the majority of human born garou probably is ready for their Rite of Passage.<br /> But it might be different from sept to sept, especially if there are lost cubs who don't want to fit in, and don't feel that what the sept has to offer is right for them. Being brought in as a lost cub is often described as brainwashing. And, sure, there are a lot of morals a human learned that now are in question. Then again new feelings and instincts rise in the cub after the first change that all more or less go in concert with the way of life and world view the sept tries to instil in the cub.<br /> <br /> While the RAW state that the tribal totem has final say over a garou joining a tribe through the rite of passage, I think this isn't meant as a loophole. Especially in LARP, where the PC Den Parent has to determine if a cub is ready (and what tribe the cub is best suited for, if no tribe can claim the cub by heritage), and has to agree with the Master of the Rite on what totem to call out for the Rite of Passage. Pushing this responsibilities away to the Totem and therefore to the ST team, is just a way of not doing what the job requires.<br /> <br /> So, in some cases the duration of the education of a cub can be longer, and harder. And while I think that there certainly are some garou who only adhere to some of a tribes defining characteristics, I too think, that some of the example character backstories or stats from the TBs don't make a lot of sense. But, the style of playing and the degree of which certain stats affect the game, varies greatly among players, so.... I give the benefit of doubt and think these things stem from a different take on the game, rather than sloppiness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T07:38:26-08:00","id":1425946,"title":"","content":"Again, this is just how I see it; But cubhood can last 2-5 years.<br /> <br /> Consider the things taught;<br /> <br /> Tribal history takes time, teaching safe shifting takes time. Learning of spirits takes time. The Litany takes time, especially the Veil protection. Nevermind teaching the lupus and metis all of this if they were previously denied.<br /> <br /> Then there are things like them learning chimanage, different rites and gifts. Combat training, using your homid/lupus form training, etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T08:46:30-08:00","id":1425965,"title":"","content":"I agree that one year isn't necessarily enough. The WoD is a terribly dangerous place and cubs need to learn combat skills, how to survive in a drastically different lifestyle, to fully understand the Gaian worldview, and to <i>unlearn</i> their human worldview (or, conversely, to drive and talk and pretend to be human). That doesn't look like just one year of teaching to me. Yet canonically Bastet kits only get one year before their mentor abandons them to sink or swim. IMO, too many would die by that system. I know that Garou traditionally designed Rites of Passage to kill half or more of their cubs, but come on. The Apocalypse is coming, why are you still killing off your cubs instead of <i>training</i> them to succeed? If your cubs die just because you didn't bother to teach them how to fight, that proves nothing about their lack of worth. And for Fera who are nearly extinct, they should have figured this out centuries or maybe millennia ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425812#post1425812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, players in general love to frontload accomplishments and achievements into their character background. And a character needs time to do that. You have to at least be in your early to mid-twenties to be combat veterans, professionals like lawyers, successful businessmen, etc. That can't be done if your PC starts at age 16. Third, people really see &quot;career/job&quot; as a defining characteristic - so their character concepts often start with that. They want certain skills, life events, and training that is unlikely to have happened to adolescents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of this is likely caused by the huge disparity between character creation and XP costs that punish you for developing a trait if you didn't start the game with 4 dots. I really wish W20 had fixed, consistent prices instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425878#post1425878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet, despite WtA being 20+ years old, we still run into this &quot;garou template/npc is a succesful in a field that requires 50% of their time&quot; issue. Which then is impossible by the stats. So, why has it not been changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>This has bugged me for a long time, because it would just be impossible for most werewolves to pull off. And yet if you don't have a job (not an average job, but one of the increasingly rare <i>really good jobs</i> that pays a real living wage) you are homeless and can barely find food. Oh and if you didn't get a high school or university education, you just can't have one of those jobs, so you better hold off your Rite of Passage until you're 19, at least.<br /> <br /> So why isn't every single Garou tribe living like the Bone Gnawers and Red Talons?) The Bone Gnawers and Red Talons should be poor because their <i>Kinfolk</i> (and hence septs) are impoverished, not just because their Garou are unemployed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425871#post1425871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pre-W20, when one could be certain if a person was a garou or a kinfolk, even pre-change, there was certainly potential for a two class upbringing of children within the kinfolk community. One out of eight (factoring in Pure Breed and talens to help with breeding true) would be a chosen warrior and certainly raised another way than their kinfolk siblings/cousins/peers. With the Curse already present, they also would need special consideration regarding their education. Public school would be difficult, but home schooling isn't an option every where. In Germany for example, school is mandatory and exceptions are rare. The number of garou wouldn't be so high as to get permits for private schools (which also may be suspicious once hunter figure that out). A boarding school might be an option, but all septs in Germany would hardly fill one school, unless kinfolk was also permitted, and even then the different tribes might object sending their kids there.<br /> <br /> Post-W20, one can't be sure if a kid is garou or not, and that leads to whole new dynamic. Does one educate all kids in a way that prepares them to be garou, or none? Starting from what age would one try to see if there are indicators of the Curse when interacting with humans? How accurate can this be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I think it's a good thing for the Baptism and Scent of the True Form to have a possibility of failure. I don't think they should succeed 100% of the time, nor fail 100% of the time. Having both options opens up more backstory possibilities for how a character was raised: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Raised as a Garou, by knowing kinfolk parents or a Garou parent.</li> <li>Raised as Kinfolk but had a surprise First Change.</li> <li>Raised in ignorance by knowing kinfolk who keep your true nature from you, but are prepared for your First hange.</li> <li>Raised in ignorance by knowing kinfolk who hide their true nature and don't expect you to Change.</li> <li>Lost Cub.</li> </ol><br /> If the Rite and Gift never fail, #2 and #4 are no longer PC options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 11-24-2020, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T09:24:19-08:00","id":1425972,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> When you wrote about Totem having the last word about cub joining the Tribe nothing clicked in my mind. Where did you find it? Because if that's true then I've been ignoring that part for over 20 years \ud83d\ude2e. From my knowledge it goes like that: <br /> 1. A Cub is found, either by Kinfetch or after more or less drastic First Change.<br /> 2. The Tribe/Sept decides which Tribe would be the best for the Cub or trades it if it isn't worthy: a Homid Cub found by Red Talons, Black Furies finding male, Silver Fangs finding someone not pure enough, Bone Gnawers someone not dirty enough. The one thing that always bothered me is what happens when Silent Striders, who are cut off from their Ancestor spirits, find somebody with good contact with a long gone Garou.<br /> 3. All the training <br /> 4. Rite of Passage <br /> 5. After successful Rite of Passage Master of Rites (or other high rank Theurge) invites the spirits and that's when the Totem begins its patronage over a pack or, if the Rite was for a single Garou, acknowledge the Cub's achieving rank of Cliath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T09:33:18-08:00","id":1425974,"title":"","content":"Bone Gnawers do not reject people for not being &quot;dirty enough&quot;. Poor people do not aspire to be dirty, that absurd. They accept anyone who is tough and willing to fight for Gaia, but most Garou refuse to join them if they have any higher status option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T09:36:45-08:00","id":1425976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425946#post1425946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this is just how I see it; But cubhood can last 2-5 years.<br /> <br /> Consider the things taught;<br /> <br /> Tribal history takes time, teaching safe shifting takes time. Learning of spirits takes time. The Litany takes time, especially the Veil protection. Nevermind teaching the lupus and metis all of this if they were previously denied.<br /> <br /> Then there are things like them learning chimanage, different rites and gifts. Combat training, using your homid/lupus form training, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still think that it wouldn't take so long. I remember what my coach said when I begun my boxing training (with self defence in my mind, I never wanted to be a pro): <br /> &quot;To do that quit after after a few months. If you stay longer I will teach you how to fight on a ring, playing by the rules. And remember, out on the streets there will be no rules&quot;.<br /> I stayed for 4 years there and I have to admit that he was right, after 3 months I begun to forget about some effective combat techniques: kicking, headbutts, using elbows, blows below the belt. And the trainings were 2 times a week, not every day like with cubs. Also I remember what was said by one of the generals who created &quot;Grom&quot;, polish special forces:<br /> &quot;Give me a man and 6 weeks, and I will get him combat ready&quot;.<br /> That's why I believe a year is enough. Besides, longer training could take away all the fun of observing the cub saying:<br /> &quot;Mommy, can I go out and kill tonight&quot; \ud83d\ude1c","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T09:39:50-08:00","id":1425978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425974#post1425974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bone Gnawers do not reject people for not being &quot;dirty enough&quot;. Poor people do not aspire to be dirty, that absurd. They accept anyone who is tough and willing to fight for Gaia, but most Garou refuse to join them if they have any higher status option.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a joke, a wordplay.\ud83d\ude42<br /> <br /> Besides I think that Scent the True Form doesn't allow you to sense the cub before First Change. If it works that way it would be too easy to find them. For homids it would be enough to check the antisocial mortals with attitude problems, for lupus the ones acting strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-24-2020, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T09:41:29-08:00","id":1425980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425965#post1425965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I think it's a good thing for the Baptism and Scent of the True Form to have a possibility of failure. I don't think they should succeed 100% of the time, nor fail 100% of the time. Having both options opens up more backstory possibilities for how a character was raised:...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that this would be the best approach, and is who we handle it in our LARP was discussed often here. Maybe, hopefully, that is the way W5 goes....<br /> <br /> So, I had a huge post on the topic, but then my browser went to the previous site and all was lost.....<br /> <br /> So, there aren't rules to &quot;unlearn&quot; things (besides ageing) but sure, the cubs have to adapt a lot of new behaviour. But should it really take several years?<br /> RAW, there is only the Instruction Skill that talks about time requirements to learn any stat. If that was applied then one had to be on the same page what dots a cliath should have in several traits to be allowed the Rite of Passage. Brawl, Dodge/Athletics for Combat. Physical attributes, too. Primal-Urge for shape shifting. But, that's it, isn't it? Subterfuge is wasted when one can't talk to humans due to the Curse - leading their thoughts on rationalisation after the Delirium might be a good help in protecting the Veil, though. Rituals is helpful, but the stance on cubs learning Rites might change from sept to sept and Den parent to Den parent. Gnosis is metaphysical, the ST has to decide if it can even be taught.<br /> <br /> It is my opinion, that once the first shift has happened any garou can shape shift. Also it is my opinion that if instructed a garou can sidestep naturally. As per the rules of shape shifting a garou with four dots in Stamina + Primal Urge will manage the shift to Crinos only in 20% of the cases, so what traits are good for a garou to become cliath?<br /> <br /> While a cub the sept will probably teach the stats that are suggested for the tribe and auspice in the core rules.<br /> <br /> As far as tribal history goes, I think that a lot will be taught &quot;as a byproduct&quot; of the 'stories and songs' phase of the monthly moots as well as gossip in the sept, but for sure there are specialised teaching sessions for the cubs, too.<br /> <br /> I think that knowledge of local spirits is also taught, as well as appropriate chiminage. But chiminage also is something that is also picked up from general story telling and current events while in the sept. Besides that some knowledge of tribal totem, the pack totems of the sept's packs (as well as guest packs) will be taught, and the caern spirit (or sept totem as per W20).<br /> <br /> The tenets of the Liatany are easily learned. If new players without tabletop WtA experience join our LARP the tenets are the first things they come into contact with and players expect that they can be recited from memory. I would argue that within the game world the cubs also only learn the tenets. Philodox and Galliard may learn stories about the Litany, too. But not all of the stories the garou dissected a dozen Millenia ago to form the tenets are still relevant today, possibly. But newer have taken their place. But they probably aren't taught in detail to all cubs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T10:05:18-08:00","id":1425986,"title":"","content":"I guess I'm only basing this off my college experience. How long does army boot camp typically last, just 6-12 months? Of course a cub needs more than boot camp, they need all the other instruction too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T10:15:30-08:00","id":1425989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425972#post1425972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> When you wrote about Totem having the last word about cub joining the Tribe nothing clicked in my mind. Where did you find it? Because if that's true then I've been ignoring that part for over 20 years \ud83d\ude2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revised Core page 63 &quot;Tribes&quot;:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When a cub undergoes the Rite of Passage, the totem of the tribe initiating him chooses whether to accept him or not \u2014 if the tribal totem approves, then the cub is part of the tribe, finally a full-fledged Garou. </div> </div> </div>The section is rewritten in W20, the passage is not there anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425972#post1425972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my knowledge it goes like that:<br /> 1. A Cub is found, either by Kinfetch or after more or less drastic First Change.<br /> 2. The Tribe/Sept decides which Tribe would be the best for the Cub or trades it if it isn't worthy: a Homid Cub found by Red Talons, Black Furies finding male, Silver Fangs finding someone not pure enough, Bone Gnawers someone not dirty enough. The one thing that always bothered me is what happens when Silent Striders, who are cut off from their Ancestor spirits, find somebody with good contact with a long gone Garou.<br /> 3. All the training<br /> 4. Rite of Passage<br /> 5. After successful Rite of Passage Master of Rites (or other high rank Theurge) invites the spirits and that's when the Totem begins its patronage over a pack or, if the Rite was for a single Garou, acknowledge the Cub's achieving rank of Cliath.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it goes this way: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Cub is found<ul><li>Either a kinfetch once bound to the kid seeks out a garou of the appropriate tribe. With the Baptism of Fire a tribe laid claim to the cub. But that might not be the case anymore in W20, since the discussed changes to the setting.</li> <li>If raised by kinfolk the cub might experience dreams and such and is brought to the garou</li> <li>The cub might just frenzy and kill whomever is there. Garou will intervene after the fact or if they employed divination Rites/Gifts even before that.</li> </ul></li> <li>Tribal affiliation is primarily determined by ancestry. But....<ul><li>if parents are from different tribes, there might be some discussion.</li> <li>if the child is not suitable for that tribe, other tribes will have to step forward</li> <li>if ancestry can't be determined (with W20 a Rite from the Get TB is moved into the general Rites category, and therefore garou could probably always determine the ancestry of a cub).</li> </ul></li> <li>The training<ul><li>if during the training the cub proofs unfit for the tribe another tribe may come forward or the garou turns Ronin. But usually one has to be very unwilling to not be suited for Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia or (if female) Black Furies.</li> </ul></li> <li>The Rite of Passage is enacted. The Ritemaster calls to the tribal totems of the tribes the cubs want to enter. While the Rite may be hard, the tribal affiliation should be a no-brainer. Since no Ritemaster would call out a Tribal Totem if he didn't believe the cub was suitable for the tribe. But sometimes other factors happen. A totem might reject a cub because of his god-like knowledge and prophetic abilities. Or the sept leader pressures the Ritemaster to send his nephew on a third Rite of passage, despite surviving two attempts by cowardice. Fenris might object, violently. Like I said, it is the garous' shared responsibility to make sure the cubs enter the tribes they fit in and how difficult the Rites of Passages are. This responsibility should not be shuffled off to the Totem (and NPC and therefore the ST).</li> <li>The Cliath might decide to join a existing pack. He succumbs to the ban of the totem, provides chiminage and therefore is allowed to spend XP on the Totem background. Or the cliath doesn't join a pack right away. Or the former cubs who went on a joined Rite of Passage decide to stay a pack, then the Rite of Totem might bind a pack Totem avatar to the pack, if the Totem accepts the pack.</li> </ol><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T10:28:31-08:00","id":1425996,"title":"","content":"Several years as a cub is something I established in my head. I don't think the books go into this in much detail, and it is something usually handwaved in games. Obviously in LARPs and online games with large player bases, some of whom start as cubs, they don't take that long before the PC graduates to Cliath - but that is essentially an OOC consideration, not something with setting justification. In those cases, Players just want to spend some time roleplaying that, and then move onto the fun stuff. I fall into Ana Mizuki's camp of 2-5 years as a cub as part of the setting (which I admit is usually not followed by PCs or character templates).<br /> <br /> I think a lot of the basic skills a Garou is supposed to know takes a few years to attain. And things like apprenticeships, service academies, military instruction, college, etc. and other preparatory instruction plus initial on-the-job training typically takes a few years. In the book, there are a lot of things like that are very concise like &quot;spend Rage&quot; - but what exactly does that mean? Channeling, directing, and controlling a supernatural power like requires some amount of time to master. And the Garou have a lot of powers like that. And things like the Litany isn't a simple 13 phrases to memorize. It's an epic poem which in its long form can take many hours to recite. And the 13 precepts are just the most important laws, not the only ones. And that's just the local version. Since every tribe and sept has its version, if one was attempting to master the Litany, that's quite a commitment. Now most cubs are probably only going to remember the basic 13 precepts once they graduate. But they'll probably be exposed to the entire thing like students in Literature class reading whole books and plays except expected to memorize much of it short term (and if you are a Philodox or Galliard, it's likely you'll be spending much of your life trying to cement it in your long term memory). I detailed a lot of that in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/383370-cub-population-in-a-sept\">a very old post here</a>.<br /> <br /> The dots in abilities are supposed to represent a kind of mastery - and we know there are general expectations of time taken to achieve that mastery. Now in practice, most games do NOT take this into consideration. If someone wants to go from 2 dots to 3 dots in a skill, the ST simply allows it to happen. Want to learn a foreign language? Spend the XP and move on. In reality, these are actually commitments that take time and effort to achieve. So if we step back from treating it like a game and treat it like an actual society, we can see that even getting that 12 year old who changed into having abilities that are ranked 2 is quite a commitment - and that's very common.<br /> <br /> Secondly, outside the abilities and powers being learned, the Garou have to indoctrinate the cub. Essentially the Garou act like a cult engaged in brainwashing. That takes time. For many cubs, everything about Garou society has to be learned in far more detail than we as PCs will ever have to do. The Litany, Silver Record, mythology stories of the spirits, displays of hierarchy and dominance have to be learned. Even Garou who were once kinfolk in a controlled community are going to learn a lot of new things. A sept will want their new Garou to be taking pride in Garou society, fanatical, and unquestioningly loyal. Many aspects of Garou will lend itself to that fellow Garou aren't affected by the Curse, they're told they're important heroes, giving personal attention and support. Those all aid things. But cubs will also have varying degrees of homesickness, preconceived ideals and values, and orneriness that will need to be overcome.<br /> <br /> There are of course variations between tribes and septs. The Fianna would be an example of a tribe with a lot of information and training they'll be dumping on a cub to master. The Bone Gnawers will likely spend a minimal time and concentrating mostly on the things needed to survive and control (like preventing Frenzy, preserving the Veil, hustling on the streets). So &quot;several years&quot; is both loose and an average.<br /> <br /> There will also be variations based on the cubs themselves. A 12 year old who changes is going to be a cub for many more years than a Lost Cub who's been an adult working in human society. That 12 year old may be a cub for 4 years or more. That guy in his late twenties might be processed in an accelerated program - not just because he already has many life skills, but because as someone used to the autonomy of being an adult, it's not practical to keep him a cub for too long.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if it is really true that cubs just need a year, we'd see character concepts in the books like a 13 year old Garou cliath NPC. And we don't. And I don't see such concepts in chronicles either. The youngest always seems to be late teens. So what about all those cubs who changed in early adolescence - perhaps as early as 10? They clearly seem to be stay as cubs for a long time. So in addition to the normal educational and indoctrination needs, there's probably some age that marks a Garou's age of maturity when they're ready to be adults and the rite of passage and they're simply not allowed to do it until then. Even the Bone Gnawers probably follow that rule. I'd say 16 is a likely candidate. I don't think people really want to see 11, 12, etc. year old Garou cliaths fighting the Wyrm because those concepts are always absent. (Now such a concept could be interesting for one NPC that may shock and compel the PCs to investigate this. It could be a great RP hook. But I think it would change the game a lot if we did see Cliaths that young as a standard.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T10:33:28-08:00","id":1425998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425980#post1425980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, there aren't rules to &amp;quot;unlearn&amp;quot; things (besides ageing) but sure, the cubs have to adapt a lot of new behaviour. But should it really take several years?<br /> RAW, there is only the Instruction Skill that talks about time requirements to learn any stat. If that was applied then one had to be on the same page what dots a cliath should have in several traits to be allowed the Rite of Passage. Brawl, Dodge/Athletics for Combat. Physical attributes, too. Primal-Urge for shape shifting. But, that's it, isn't it? Subterfuge is wasted when one can't talk to humans due to the Curse - leading their thoughts on rationalisation after the Delirium might be a good help in protecting the Veil, though. Rituals is helpful, but the stance on cubs learning Rites might change from sept to sept and Den parent to Den parent. Gnosis is metaphysical, the ST has to decide if it can even be taught</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah. That's funny cause it's hard for me to imagine an average teenager without Subterfuge AT LEAST 2 \ud83d\ude01.<br /> <br /> And what is RAW?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T10:36:47-08:00","id":1425999,"title":"","content":"RAW is an acronym for &quot;Rules as written&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T10:39:51-08:00","id":1426002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425986#post1425986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm only basing this off my college experience. How long does army boot camp typically last, just 6-12 months? Of course a cub needs more than boot camp, they need all the other instruction too.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my country, when there was a draft, during the Warsaw Pact it was 2 years (3 in the Navy), later it was 1 year (2 in the Navy) and, before our army change its profile to professional, it was reduced to 9 months regardless of type. But I believe the general I've mentioned that it would take about 6 weeks to train a soldier. He's an elite so he knows what he's talking about. The rest of the time was spent on learning ranks, marching etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T10:55:28-08:00","id":1426010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425986#post1425986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm only basing this off my college experience. How long does army boot camp typically last, just 6-12 months? Of course a cub needs more than boot camp, they need all the other instruction too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boot camp is simply Basic Training. That is some simple indoctrination, getting people into physical shape, and very basic skills training. That's ten weeks.<br /> <br /> THEN recruits go to Advanced Individual Training where they learn their actual JOBS they'll be doing in the military. That's six to twelve more months.<br /> <br /> Recruits selected for the hardest occupations (say running the nuclear engines on a supercarrier or submarine) take even longer. They won't leave until two years after they enlist (at least in the US military).<br /> <br /> But of course, military recruits don't join when they are ages 10-16 like when Garou have their first change. They join after high school graduation when they've already acquired a certain amount of knowledge and skill. A high school education isn't much, but it should still reflect 1 dot ranks in Abilities like Academics, Computer, Drive, and possibly Science, Technology, Crafts, Athletics, Leadership, and Expression among others. And likely a few more abilities from hobbies and life experience. The military has standards too - and prospective recruits who fail certain standards don't get accepted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T11:10:17-08:00","id":1426013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425965#post1425965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has bugged me for a long time, because it would just be impossible for most werewolves to pull off. And yet if you don't have a job (not an average job, but one of the increasingly rare <i>really good jobs</i> that pays a real living wage) you are homeless and can barely find food. Oh and if you didn't get a high school or university education, you just can't have one of those jobs, so you better hold off your Rite of Passage until you're 19, at least.<br /> <br /> So why isn't every single Garou tribe living like the Bone Gnawers and Red Talons?) The Bone Gnawers and Red Talons should be poor because their <i>Kinfolk</i> (and hence septs) are impoverished, not just because their Garou are unemployed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Kinfolk, rejection of human life entirely and septs/Caerns. Like I've said multiple times in this thread, the kinfolk are the backbone of the Garou Nation. All the fancy things Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords have? Kinfolk owned. Everything they have is bought or made by their kin and so they can focus on being garou. Why should you bother living in squalor when you have people waiting hand and foot to aid you? That is why they are not living like Gnawers and Talons. They live comfy in their septs, supported by their kinfolk.<br /> <br /> This is why Glass Walkers in revised TB are said to have such difficult time with their kin, as the garou already do most of the jobs the kinfolk do. Leave the kin doing the shit jobs left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T11:48:17-08:00","id":1426021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1425996#post1425996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several years as a cub is something I established in my head. I don't think the books go into this in much detail, and it is something usually handwaved in games. Obviously in LARPs and online games with large player bases, some of whom start as cubs, they don't take that long before the PC graduates to Cliath - but that is essentially an OOC consideration, not something with setting justification. In those cases, Players just want to spend some time roleplaying that, and then move onto the fun stuff. I fall into Ana Mizuki's camp of 2-5 years as a cub as part of the setting (which I admit is usually not followed by PCs or character templates).<br /> <br /> I think a lot of the basic skills a Garou is supposed to know takes a few years to attain. And things like apprenticeships, service academies, military instruction, college, etc. and other preparatory instruction plus initial on-the-job training typically takes a few years. In the book, there are a lot of things like that are very concise like &amp;quot;spend Rage&amp;quot; - but what exactly does that mean? Channeling, directing, and controlling a supernatural power like requires some amount of time to master. And the Garou have a lot of powers like that. And things like the Litany isn't a simple 13 phrases to memorize. It's an epic poem which in its long form can take many hours to recite. And the 13 precepts are just the most important laws, not the only ones. And that's just the local version. Since every tribe and sept has its version, if one was attempting to master the Litany, that's quite a commitment. Now most cubs are probably only going to remember the basic 13 precepts once they graduate. But they'll probably be exposed to the entire thing like students in Literature class reading whole books and plays except expected to memorize much of it short term (and if you are a Philodox or Galliard, it's likely you'll be spending much of your life trying to cement it in your long term memory). I detailed a lot of that in <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/383370-cub-population-in-a-sept&amp;quot;]a</a> very old post here[/URL].<br /> <br /> The dots in abilities are supposed to represent a kind of mastery - and we know there are general expectations of time taken to achieve that mastery. Now in practice, most games do NOT take this into consideration. If someone wants to go from 2 dots to 3 dots in a skill, the ST simply allows it to happen. Want to learn a foreign language? Spend the XP and move on. In reality, these are actually commitments that take time and effort to achieve. So if we step back from treating it like a game and treat it like an actual society, we can see that even getting that 12 year old who changed into having abilities that are ranked 2 is quite a commitment - and that's very common.<br /> <br /> Secondly, outside the abilities and powers being learned, the Garou have to indoctrinate the cub. Essentially the Garou act like a cult engaged in brainwashing. That takes time. For many cubs, everything about Garou society has to be learned in far more detail than we as PCs will ever have to do. The Litany, Silver Record, mythology stories of the spirits, displays of hierarchy and dominance have to be learned. Even Garou who were once kinfolk in a controlled community are going to learn a lot of new things. A sept will want their new Garou to be taking pride in Garou society, fanatical, and unquestioningly loyal. Many aspects of Garou will lend itself to that fellow Garou aren't affected by the Curse, they're told they're important heroes, giving personal attention and support. Those all aid things. But cubs will also have varying degrees of homesickness, preconceived ideals and values, and orneriness that will need to be overcome.<br /> <br /> There are of course variations between tribes and septs. The Fianna would be an example of a tribe with a lot of information and training they'll be dumping on a cub to master. The Bone Gnawers will likely spend a minimal time and concentrating mostly on the things needed to survive and control (like preventing Frenzy, preserving the Veil, hustling on the streets). So &amp;quot;several years&amp;quot; is both loose and an average.<br /> <br /> There will also be variations based on the cubs themselves. A 12 year old who changes is going to be a cub for many more years than a Lost Cub who's been an adult working in human society. That 12 year old may be a cub for 4 years or more. That guy in his late twenties might be processed in an accelerated program - not just because he already has many life skills, but because as someone used to the autonomy of being an adult, it's not practical to keep him a cub for too long.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if it is really true that cubs just need a year, we'd see character concepts in the books like a 13 year old Garou cliath NPC. And we don't. And I don't see such concepts in chronicles either. The youngest always seems to be late teens. So what about all those cubs who changed in early adolescence - perhaps as early as 10? They clearly seem to be stay as cubs for a long time. So in addition to the normal educational and indoctrination needs, there's probably some age that marks a Garou's age of maturity when they're ready to be adults and the rite of passage and they're simply not allowed to do it until then. Even the Bone Gnawers probably follow that rule. I'd say 16 is a likely candidate. I don't think people really want to see 11, 12, etc. year old Garou cliaths fighting the Wyrm because those concepts are always absent. (Now such a concept could be interesting for one NPC that may shock and compel the PCs to investigate this. It could be a great RP hook. But I think it would change the game a lot if we did see Cliaths that young as a standard.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In general I can agree with you. Learning a foreign language isn't easy. But, on the other hand, statistically to understand 75% of foreign language you need about 800 words. Average person uses 3000-5000 during words day-to-day activity. The rest is grammar. And even that could be reduced. In Poland, during english classes, I was taught many grammar skills which I never use. In turn most of my vocabulary comes from Cartoon Network, MTV and Eurosport, before they got polish version. Also you talk about Knowledges. Take Talents instead:<br /> &quot;Don't put your thumb inside your fist when you punch something or you'll break it&quot;<br /> Puff, you got your first dot of Brawl.<br /> <br /> As for indoctrination I think that there is not much to do. Most of prechange teens are already shoved aside by their peers so they would gladly accept anyone who show them interest (I remember myself as a young teenager). The hardest part is convince them not to use their newfound abilities to avenge school injustices.<br /> <br /> I think also that 12 years old will need less time to adapt than a 20 years old (maybe except those raised outside the Kinfolk society). First of all their minds are more flexible. Second, they usually have more free time (6 hrs of school vs at least 8 hrs of college/work). Ok, adults can have their free time after the mythical 10PM, but Kinfolks who raised the cub usually won't mind them returning late (as if they have any choice). But I think that average age of a Cub ready for Rite of Passage is about 14-16. Besides long training could be used in Dark Ages, when Wyrm was weak and the BSDs were almost nonextistent. In modern times I doubt that any Sept have time to teach their cubs about all the complexities of Litany. Besides, longer training raises the chance of finding another cub on your protectorate so that means that either the teachers have to divide their time between their pupils or cut down the training time of a newer one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T12:13:14-08:00","id":1426028,"title":"","content":"<span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span><br /> Regarding the &quot;Rite of Passage&quot; it is not entirely clear what the garou do. The &quot;Rite of Passage&quot; 1st Edition adventure had a full page with a dialogue of between the Rite Master and the returning cubs that are supposed to be the ritual words before the cubs tell the tale of the Rite and then the sept deems them worhty or not. But, as a LARPer we have to get more actual doing into the Rite, so while not written in the rules, it is a fair assumption that Rite of Passage starts with a proclamation. So the sept comes together, around the fire, the Den parent states, that in his opinion the cub or cubs are ready to undergo the rites of passage. If there were mentors/teachers specifically for tribe or auspice matter they will give short testimony and if no objections are formulated, the Ritemaster starts the Rite, naming the cubs, which tribes they want to proof themselves worthy of joining. Then the mission might be given and everyone is reminded that no outside help is allowed. At this point the Ritemaster might (or might not) also call out to the spirits in general to bless the Rite and the Tribal Totems of the tribes in question specifically - for the deeds during the Rite are done by the cubs to proof their worth to them too.<br /> Like I said, it isn't described in the books, but that's how we play it in the LARP, because we can't just handwave this essential part, where all PCs are involved, just like the return of the cubs where the ritual dialogue is held. Also, after the cubs tell their tale, they leave the scene so the PCs of rank can in a semi-InPlay-semi-OutOfCharacter discussion come up with deed names for the Cliaths. After that the cubs return and are given their names and thereby enter the tribes, too. If a tribal totem was to objects, it would have intervened by some means by now.<br /> <br /> But that whole process has nothing to do with the Rite of Totem, that binds a pack and a totem. Except that we require a pack to only have members of at least cliath rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T15:29:00-08:00","id":1426045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1426021#post1426021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take Talents instead:<br /> &quot;Don't put your thumb inside your fist when you punch something or you'll break it&quot;<br /> Puff, you got your first dot of Brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Talents aren't developed by book learning, but that doesn't mean they don't take time to master. Talents require practice. The rules for many sports and other athletics are often very simple. That doesn't mean athletes don't spend a lot of time honing their skills, developing muscle memory, conditioning their bodies, and advancing their mastery. They put in a lot of training.<br /> <br /> I'd consider equivalents to first dot of Brawl to be high school students with several seasons of competitive wrestling, or several years of classes at their local martial arts school. They've studied the basics and mastered many of the technical skills required, but still have a long way to apply them in novel situations or developed the internal discipline and mental fortitude needed for the next rank. However, I imagine that children who have long played sports competitively in their age group have either achieved their second dot of Athletics or Brawl or are near it by the time they graduate high school. These are the people most likely to continue to compete in such sports in college and beyond.<br /> <br /> This by itself doesn't need to take so long especially if it is a subject the cub is very interested in. But once you realize <i>all</i> the things a cub needs to be a functional adult among the Garou, they add up. If you want that cub to become immersed with Garou culture, master all the supernatural powers, and have dots in common abilities like Alertness, Athletics, Brawl, Intimidation, Subterfuge, Primal-Urge, Firearms, Melee, Stealth, Survival, Enigmas, Occult and Rituals, you have some school years there. And many of these abilities are going to be raised to the second dot.<br /> <br /> This is just a general average. Some tribes are going to be much more strict in what they expect from their cubs (the Get will emphasize combat; the Fianna cultural and physical excellence, the Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords leadership; the Stargazers will have a heavy intellectual and philosophical approach), and then you have the Bone Gnawers who won't teach anywhere near as much. But they're just as likely to be lazy about teaching the little they do, so who knows that may take a lot longer than you'd be expect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1426021#post1426021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think also that 12 years old will need less time to adapt than a 20 years old (maybe except those raised outside the Kinfolk society).</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't about making sure kids adapt to the new lifestyle. It's about conditioning them to accept unhesitatingly Garou cultural values so by the time they become adults, they don't question things. Being Garou is very stressful for a variety of reasons. Once exposed to the world outside the sept again, the Garou in question might come into contact with many people and experiences that could cause them to question Garou values and their commitment to them. When that happens, you want them to instinctively reject those ideas. And the way you do that is providing a comprehensive education they can go back on which answers anything that provoke doubts (or at least causes them to go, &quot;I know we're right and they're wrong but I'm having trouble articulating why; I'll go back to my mentor and ask - I should have paid more attention as a cub&quot;). You have to install it early on. If it is done too superficially, those ideals and values won't hold up under pressure or exposure to other ideas. It's why totalitarian states have the Hitler Youth, Red Pioneers, and Red Guards.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you run the risk of those idealistic, loyal Cliaths becoming jaded, confused Fostern who ask a lot of embarrassing questions and want to think for themselves instead of finding the answer in Garou culture. The entire culture could fall apart. Garou breeding with Garou. Tolerating man eaters. Not killing high Humanity vampires. Allowing the aged and infirm to become a burden to the sept. Dogs and cats living together. Mass hysteria. Real Bone Gnawer stuff.<br /> <br /> It is even more important to train young cubs, because those are your best bet for future fanatics who hold the line and enforce orthodoxy. Those Lost Cubs are going to bring in a lot of ideas they already hold from their human lives. They can't be entirely trusted. It's easy to see them slipping back to bad habits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1426021#post1426021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In modern times I doubt that any Sept have time to teach their cubs about all the complexities of Litany. Besides, longer training raises the chance of finding another cub on your protectorate so that means that either the teachers have to divide their time between their pupils or cut down the training time of a newer one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most cubs likely learn a condensed version of the Litany, but probably more than just the 13 precepts. And certainly some cubs are going to have to study this in depth. You want Philodox cubs to be well grounded. Whether or not that Garou takes their first or second dot in Law is balanced among many other things. Just like not all cubs are going to learn Rituals or specific Rites. But all of them probably get exposed to it, and certain auspices are definitely going to devote time to it. All the auspices are going to be prepared to fulfill their role.<br /> <br /> And it's not like when Garou are cubs that they aren't doing anything productive. They're given all the menial and boring work around the sept. They provide free labor to those mentoring them so they can &quot;learn on the job&quot;. They can assist the Guardians as look outs and scouts. They're not ready for war yet, but they can still earn their keep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1426021#post1426021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think that average age of a Cub ready for Rite of Passage is about 14-16.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it is average, but if some Garou change when they're 10, then certainly a Rite of Passage around 14-16 provides them plenty of time to learn what they need. If a cub changes when they're 16, they probably go on their Rite of Passage later between 18-20.<br /> <br /> I will say, I'm now interested in running an NPC who changed when she was 10 and is now a Cliath Ahroun at age 14 just to see how the PCs react. At 14, the Cliath still has several more years of puberty left. I imagine most of my players will think that's too early to start fighting the Wyrm and it might lead to some interesting roleplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T15:53:52-08:00","id":1426048,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13141\" data-vbnamecard=\"13141\">Nail Eater</a> one of your posts on this page broke the forum somehow. Could you please check to see if you left a tag open or anything like that?<br /> <br /> I think Nail Eater is right that Glass Walkers are less picky than Black Furies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1426013#post1426013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinfolk, rejection of human life entirely and septs/Caerns. Like I've said multiple times in this thread, the kinfolk are the backbone of the Garou Nation. All the fancy things Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords have? Kinfolk owned. Everything they have is bought or made by their kin and so they can focus on being garou. Why should you bother living in squalor when you have people waiting hand and foot to aid you? That is why they are not living like Gnawers and Talons. They live comfy in their septs, supported by their kinfolk.<br /> <br /> This is why Glass Walkers in revised TB are said to have such difficult time with their kin, as the garou already do most of the jobs the kinfolk do. Leave the kin doing the shit jobs left.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you, but the RAW totally contradicts this common sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T23:39:57-08:00","id":1426084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1426048#post1426048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I agree with you, but the RAW totally contradicts this common sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is RAW, as much as it is &quot;this is the thing our writers came up with, using this setting.&quot; It is the same reason why so many WtA novels leave out game critical facts such as challenges and Rage. For example, I think Song of the UnMaking is the first WtA novel I've read that actually uses most of the setting stuff such as Rage, challenges, gifts, rites and auspices.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T00:21:31-08:00","id":1426087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enrinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">one of your posts on this page broke the forum somehow. Could you please check to see if you left a tag open or anything like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder how in the world he did this, lol. He must be a Marauder for somehow breaking the reality of the site.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T02:45:39-08:00","id":1426098,"title":"","content":"About the young Garous:<br /> One of my friend's favourite character was a 13-14 year old Silent Strider Ragabash Cliath. It was an intresting RP. He both played the naivety and lack of moral well. It was also intresting when he was a higher Rank, than a much older Garou. He was deadly with Fang Dagger. Unfortunately his skull was smashed into pieces by a silvered knuckles.<br /> <br /> My main character (metis) started in the biological age 14. Now he's 20, but experienced more than anybody should. It took years of real time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T12:46:10-08:00","id":1426162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1426087#post1426087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder how in the world he did this, lol. He must be a Marauder for somehow breaking the reality of the site.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neh, only a Glass Walker with a Jinxed flaw \ud83d\ude1c.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T13:08:41-08:00","id":1426166,"title":"","content":"It's your post where you quoted Heinrich. You made a typo somewhere in the quote tags.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T13:22:01-08:00","id":1426170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1426045#post1426045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. Talents aren't developed by book learning, but that doesn't mean they don't take time to master. Talents require practice. The rules for many sports and other athletics are often very simple. That doesn't mean athletes don't spend a lot of time honing their skills, developing muscle memory, conditioning their bodies, and advancing their mastery. They put in a lot of training.<br /> <br /> I'd consider equivalents to first dot of Brawl to be high school students with several seasons of competitive wrestling, or several years of classes at their local martial arts school. They've studied the basics and mastered many of the technical skills required, but still have a long way to apply them in novel situations or developed the internal discipline and mental fortitude needed for the next rank. However, I imagine that children who have long played sports competitively in their age group have either achieved their second dot of Athletics or Brawl or are near it by the time they graduate high school. These are the people most likely to continue to compete in such sports in college and beyond.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, you are right. Rulebooks state that two dots means average, regularly trained human. I can agree with that. On the other hand I've been training boxing for about 4 years and believe me, learning how to hit, hurt your opponent not injuring yourself durong the process is easier than you think. The same I think about driving, melee or foreign languages. On the other hand my engineering skills (that means everything, from simple repairs at home to computer use) are still abysmal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1426045#post1426045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't about making sure kids adapt to the new lifestyle. It's about conditioning them to accept unhesitatingly Garou cultural values so by the time they become adults, they don't question things. Being Garou is very stressful for a variety of reasons. Once exposed to the world outside the sept again, the Garou in question might come into contact with many people and experiences that could cause them to question Garou values and their commitment to them. When that happens, you want them to instinctively reject those ideas. And the way you do that is providing a comprehensive education they can go back on which answers anything that provoke doubts (or at least causes them to go, &amp;quot;I know we're right and they're wrong but I'm having trouble articulating why; I'll go back to my mentor and ask - I should have paid more attention as a cub&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. You have to install it early on. If it is done too superficially, those ideals and values won't hold up under pressure or exposure to other ideas. It's why totalitarian states have the Hitler Youth, Red Pioneers, and Red Guards.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you run the risk of those idealistic, loyal Cliaths becoming jaded, confused Fostern who ask a lot of embarrassing questions and want to think for themselves instead of finding the answer in Garou culture. The entire culture could fall apart. Garou breeding with Garou. Tolerating man eaters. Not killing high Humanity vampires. Allowing the aged and infirm to become a burden to the sept. Dogs and cats living together. Mass hysteria. Real Bone Gnawer stuff.<br /> <br /> It is even more important to train young cubs, because those are your best bet for future fanatics who hold the line and enforce orthodoxy. Those Lost Cubs are going to bring in a lot of ideas they already hold from their human lives. They can't be entirely trusted. It's easy to see them slipping back to bad habits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but you're talking about fanaticism. And there are two things you can be sure about fanatics: they are completely devoid of free will and cannot think rationally. I doubt the Garou as a whole want to train a mindless army of psycho killers. If that's so I think they will be long dead. Sometimes you have to spare the wyrmspawn (if only to extract the intel). If it was like you wrote I think that there won't be Valkenburg Foundation, Monkeywrenches, Renewalists Silver Fangs camp and Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers will be no more as too weaverish. Ok, there are many fanatics among Garou, but on the other hand you have Fangs of Garm, who are more like an average Ahroun of Children of Gaia than average Get. Hell, my own Children of Gaia Ahroun is more aggressive than Garms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1426045#post1426045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if it is average, but if some Garou change when they're 10, then certainly a Rite of Passage around 14-16 provides them plenty of time to learn what they need. If a cub changes when they're 16, they probably go on their Rite of Passage later between 18-20.<br /> <br /> I will say, I'm now interested in running an NPC who changed when she was 10 and is now a Cliath Ahroun at age 14 just to see how the PCs react. At 14, the Cliath still has several more years of puberty left. I imagine most of my players will think that's too early to start fighting the Wyrm and it might lead to some interesting roleplay.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's average. I have to admit that I based my opinion on templates bios and pictures. They should be treated either as cubs ready for their Rite of Passage or Cliaths just after it. On the other hand, if we treat video games as canon in that (and I think we should, cause some members of WW acted as creators of them) then we will have one 16 years old tribeless cub, who is recognized as Cliath after the entire game (from unreleased Heart of Gaia) and 24 years old, freshly changed Garou who pass the Rite of Passage without knowing Litany, Gifts even its own Tribe (from Heart of the Forest). So that could mean we're both right. Or wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T13:26:13-08:00","id":1426171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1426166#post1426166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's your post where you quoted Heinrich. You made a typo somewhere in the quote tags.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think you're right. Still I don't know how to fix it. I can try but as I wrote, I'm Jinxed so the results can be even worse \ud83d\ude14.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T15:12:35-08:00","id":1426182,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I think I got it fixed. Sorry I had to delete them. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T15:25:57-08:00","id":1426184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1426182#post1426182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I think I got it fixed. Sorry I had to delete them. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I think that most active users of this thread already read it so nothing to worry about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-26-2020, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T20:11:28-08:00","id":1426194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1426170#post1426170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but you're talking about fanaticism. And there are two things you can be sure about fanatics: they are completely devoid of free will and cannot think rationally. I doubt the Garou as a whole want to train a mindless army of psycho killers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to get into a debate about semantics of the term 'fanatic'. (I think it's a complete mistake to think fanatics don't have free will or can't think rationally. They do. It's just they have dogma that they won't challenge - and dogma can be limited to certain areas, but not others.) But I will try again to explain my meaning. I am not talking about Garou slaughtering everyone. It's about preserving their culture. They have preserved a minority culture in secret among humans for thousand and thousands of years. Preserving a minority culture is not easy. Real world human cultures aren't preserved for that long. Minority cultures that exist in a sea of foreign cultures are even harder. You need to establish a lot of pride, a strong group identity, establish strict taboos and regulations that prevent your culture from being subsumed from the surrounding people. This, in part, is a reason why the Garou are a very ritualized society.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk culture has changed radically over time because ultimately they are part of human culture. But actual Garou culture much less so. There should be a stronger continuity with the Garou over say the last 10,000 years than there would be among their kinfolk.<br /> <br /> It takes work to achieve that. They need to inundate their cubs with history, stories, myth, mores, and values. That requires a certain amount of time.<br /> <br /> They have to turn that human runaway that just arrived into a Garou of their tribe. They don't want to run the risk of that runaway remaining a human American with 21st century values who just happens to have the powers of a Garou because that human American is going to subvert a Garou culture that's last 10,000 (even longer in some versions) with their modern American values (or their Medieval Christian values, or their Muslim Arab values or Parthian Zoroastrian values, etc.) This difficulty is probably one reason there are a lot more Ronin now than they were previously, and why half the Bone Gnawers are supposed to be &quot;Rabble&quot;. It's a lot harder now to indoctrinate new Garou because of the mass media, information technology, and universal education.<br /> <br /> That runaway is already going to have certain ideas about human and political rights, the value of human life, what a fair trial means, what justice looks like, a predefine notion of honor, and many other things that will conflict with the Litany and Garou culture. The Garou need to obliterate that and reprogram that person. That means summoning enough evidence, facts, logic, arguments, etc. to overcome expected objections. The time to do that is when they are a cub, because once they pass the Rite of Passage they're now adults who can make their own decisions. So the Garou need enough time to educate someone so they can become a Garou culturally. They have to indoctrinate them.<br /> <br /> I think that takes a long time - more than several months or even a year.<br /> <br /> I've gone on at length about this, and think I've said everything I could to explain my position. Not much to add. Feel free to continue to comment, but rather than keep repeating myself and preventing the thread from moving on, I'll try to make this my last post on this thread about this subject. I think it's been a good discussion and hope people have found benefit in it. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T01:05:05-08:00","id":1426211,"title":"","content":"But, depending on tribe, their culture isn't 10.000years old. Not by a long shot. And it is constantly changing.<br /> <br /> I totally agree that garou will try to instil the group identity and sense of belonging into any lost cubs. To some degree also to kinfolk. Besides the tribal identity, there is also the sept identity. Tribal identity takes step back, when there is a multi-tribal sept, because more concessions need to be made to make everyday life work.<br /> <br /> But, in the Setting there is always the mention of discrepancies on young garous' vs. old garous' world views and also that the culture became to homid-esque for the decreasing number of lupus born garou. And some tribes have multiple characteristics that are deemed fundamental (or clich\u00e9) for that tribe. Certain cubs will be welcomed into the tribe who excel at some of these characteristics, but not on all.<br /> <br /> A young Black Fury for example might wholeheartedly defend female and infants, and fight for each and everyone's personal freedoms but just not be into a 'wyld'-ish lifestyle. And, since all the tribes draw there inspiration from human cultures (the one's the kinfolk of these tribes stems from), the tribes have characteristics that surely were integrated into the tribe simply because they could not protect the tribes completely from the change of time and changes in human culture.<br /> <br /> Do garou make an effort there, sure. Are they succeeding, only kinda. So, it is fair to assume that their indoctrination of cubs is partly flawed...<br /> Not to mention that the cubs also could employ Subterfuge to get trough the process with some of their human society habits and believes still intact. Sure, the garou have Empathy to counter, but statistically some cubs would get away with it...<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Or change their views back to a more human standard after the Rite of Passage, due to contact with humans or kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 11-26-2020, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T03:48:28-08:00","id":1426222,"title":"","content":"Logic. Logic has so many facets as there are inteligent beings (not trying to offend any living creature). Just as it was written in old STs Handbook (I believe 2nd edition): Garou have fun thinking about humans who still view USA divided to North and South. Their laugh is stopped when they recall themselves War of Rage or the division between pro- and anti-Impergium Garou. And still, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> wrote there are many old fashioned Garou who would likely ignite those once again.<br /> <br /> As for human cultures there are many who are as old as Garou. And I don't have those 10000 years, because this culture is no more. During that time the tribes emerge from a race as a whole, Wars of Rage and War of Tears erupted, Impergium ended. And the culture has changed, influenced sometimes by Kinfolks (like Fianna by Finn McCool) sometimes even mere mortals. Look at the Sikhs, south american Indians or Aborigins, they still practice their old customs and beliefs. Ok, sometimes as a tourist trap but still. And there isn't much difference between them and Mother Larissa telling the Garou stories (censored of course) to the kids at Central Park.<br /> <br /> As for indoctrination the human culture does the same, trying to instill certain values into its members. In Poland I can see it very clearly. You know &quot;40:1&quot; by Sabaton? About polish commander who bravely fought the Germans during WWII. There was not a word about him during all my entire education. In my country only 3 cities have a street of his name. In my hometown a renamed street has John Wayne as a patron (instead of a socialist patron, whose only flaw was that he believed in comunism before Stalin purges had started). Instead in almost any city has a street named after a field marshall, who before WWII spent the money for unpractical means of defence, and then, in September 39 bravely fled the country. I was taught that liberum veto was wrong. Then why my country was then at the peak of its power? So I think that if a cub can think freely there still be many questions about Garou culture. Not to mention that it's hard to change the point of view after 16 years of human brainwashing. What will Garou do if the cub oppose? Beat him to a pulp?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T07:58:32-08:00","id":1426237,"title":"","content":"I have to agree that deprogramming human values will take time, probably more than 1 year. Homid cubs are raised to believe <i>very strongly</i> in things like Capitalism and Monotheistic religions and Science, and a hatred of predatory animals. They won't give up these worldviews quickly or easily or willingly, even after the First Change and a glimpse of the Umbra upends their lives. And even before when most humans were polytheists or ancestor-venerators and could comprehend the existence of a goddess like Gaia, most human cultures still probably taught their kids to unquestionably assume that humans are superior and have a right to rule over and control nature, that humans are the Most Important On Earth and that animals and plants don't count as people. There are certainly human cultures that didn't teach that -- several Native American cultures for example -- and I suspect that Human-First worldview was less prevelant among hunter-gatherers and fisher-gatherers.<br /> <br /> These human worldviews don't just threaten Garou customs and traditions. They are a huge threat to Gaia. They are a big reason most humans and mages want to &quot;tame&quot; nature and shoot dangerous animals to extinction. A Garou cannot whole-heartedly defend Gaia, and truly accept themselves as an inhuman monster, if they cling to human values.<br /> <br /> The Glasswalkers may not care about driving out this human thinking, and the Red Talons don't have to, but every other tribe should be very concerned to get that poison out before it turns their cubs and cliath into traitors to Gaia. They can't afford half-measures and incomplete deprogramming.<br /> <br /> The irony is that to some extent this is their own faults. IMO, if they hadn't turned the Ratkin's version of Impergium into a public slaughter-fest, if they hadn't massacred all the Gurahl and Apis who were teaching humans to respect Gaia, humans (in the WoD) would have more respect for Gaia, and less fear and hatred of nature and wild animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 11-26-2020, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T07:59:07-08:00","id":1426238,"title":"","content":"If a cub doesn't fall in line? Well, that's where Ronins come from if the tribe is more liberal, or how cubs die, if the tribe is more traditional.<br /> Shadow Lords might employ brain washing tactics that could border on torture, i guess.<br /> But other tribes won't. Specifically the Get of Fenris have a strong opinion against violence against the young. Beating them into submission is the same as raising cowards. Get have to be strong in will and choose to face the hardships of their physical training.<br /> <br /> I can see extreme views regarding tradition with the young and the old. Some young will hear tales of the old times and mistake them for glorious times - aiming to be strict and traditional out of this misconception. Others will think the old ways failed because of the state the world is in now and refuse to life by these old ways.<br /> Older garou also have formed stronger opinions over the years and might be extremists in one direction or the other...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T22:09:51-08:00","id":1426284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1423708-definition-of-being-garou?p=1426238#post1426238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a cub doesn't fall in line?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a variety of responses depending on how much the cub seems to reject Garou culture. This, like all things, varies among tribes and septs.<br /> <br /> The most favorable is that the cub completes the rite of passage and is accepted by his tribe. But others keep watch on him to see how he acts, and they may be quicker than usual to perform rites of Punishment, proclaim scandal for Renown loss, scapegoated for problems, forced to wait longer to be awarded renown, and use other social means to deter him from voicing or acting hostile opinions. So he could be ostracized to a certain extent. This approach may be combined with a carrot and stick approach to encourage him to &quot;reform&quot; his views. But the point of everything is to get him to better confirm to the group's norms.<br /> <br /> The Garou might perform a &quot;Code Red&quot; - very coercive measures (perhaps done by others as to not implicate the sept or tribal leadership or violate the Litany) to straighten out the Garou. As Heinrich mentioned, this does not fit all tribes, but still fits a lot of them. This would involve things like physical abuse, torture (although that tribe may not define it as torture), deprivation, etc. Mental or social coercion might also be used. This could also be the exact opposite - set a lot of carrots before the cub (as long as it does not cause envy by more well behaved cubs). They might encourage an attractive kinfolk to show interest; demonstrate how being a proper Garou will lead to Gifts, powers, and aid to help them accomplish some goa, or some other tangible benefit to cooperating. Bribery, blackmail, etc. would be engaged.<br /> <br /> Another option is to bump him down to the Bone Gnawers because they're already worthless. Maybe he can do some good there, and if not, the Gnawers could hardly do worse at this point, and they're already despised by the other tribes. - Give the cub a train ticket to New York and tell her to find Mother Larissa in Central Park. She'll know what to do with her.<br /> <br /> A possibility is that they get sent into temporary exile and remain - essentially - a Lost Cub. The intention is that the burden of being alone will straighten the cub out, and he'll come back properly chastised. Maybe not at this sept, but another one. It's a risk because he might be killed or recruited by the BSDs, but I think any local septs will evaluate the risks before doing this.<br /> <br /> Then there is the Rite of the Lone Wolf - making them Ronin. I think this, ironically, would require them to succeed on a Rite of Passage first (the sept may simply perform the Rite as opposed to sending them on an actual quest to be tested). It's a Punishment, and I don't think that can be applied to cubs. I imagine in most cases this is more the decision of the cub than other Garou. The difference between this and the previous option is that the status of Ronin is one of permanent exile.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the tribe that claims the cub kills her, but again only after performing the Rite of Passage. The adventure Rite of Passage makes it clear the Litany prevents this, and any death penalties can only happen if the cub is an adult. A variation is to send the cub on a dangerous rite of passage quest in the hopes it'll kill her. I think this is the most extreme and would only be done in exceptional circumstances - the cub expressed interest in joining the BSDs, engaged in man eating, or some other capital crime.<br /> <br /> I think cubs that don't fall in line are much more likely to be Lost Cubs who were found as adults rather than small children. The younger the child, the easier to indoctrinate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T22:48:33-08:00","id":1426289,"title":"","content":"Basically I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>.<br /> In our LARP game PCs wouldn't trust a cub to take a train to anywhere alone, especially if the cub is not behaving. They would send cliaths to take care of the transfer. In anything happened the Den Parent would be responsible.<br /> <br /> Also, if there was never a Rite of Passage the Rite of Lone Wolf doesn't seem to apply. I mean one could perform it, for being a ritualised society, though. But I would call garou, who fail to have a Rite of Passage Ronin, just like those who basically had the Rite of Passage revoked by the Lone Wolf. 'Lost Cub', for me, doesn't fit once the cub has had some level of training. But I think there aren't definitions in the rules.<br /> <br /> There are lone garou who live at the brink of protectorates and are tolerated by the local sept(s). This can be garou who are unwilling to life the garou lifestyle...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-27T00:23:50-08:00","id":1426293,"title":"","content":"I also think that with the First Change by itself, the new cub practically NEEDS Garou society as adequate support at this point. Garou as a default aren't human (nor the wolf if their natural breedform is Lupus instead of Homid) and with their innate rage, have trouble making common ground with human society; especially after the point of First Change like I mentioned earlier. I can only see a Garou splitting off (becoming Ronin) from the Nation as a whole when they've gathered some years of natural survival skills for it to be viable.. but a cub on its own, confused entirely about its entire new found identity? ...I don't know about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-27T02:37:58-08:00","id":1426301,"title":"","content":"Well, I could think of lost cubs (homid and lupus) who fend for themselves. Also with spirit or kinfolk as their sole advidors - and for more stranger origins stories with Fera or Changeling support. They would try to make sense of what they experience and what they feel and work through it.<br /> <br /> That said, there is a get of fenris cub, who failed his Gnosis roll on first drinking vitae and become a ghoul and later bodyguard to the prince. After camarilla and Sabbat killed each other off he was the last one standing and is ruling as a Prince now - supposedly with Camarilla support. Iirc, it is a otherwise not noteworthy town in Ireland, where this has happened. And an anti-example of what you get, when you let Changeling Sourcebooks define WtA/VtM background <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-27T07:14:59-08:00","id":1426314,"title":"","content":"I thought that character was an Abomination, not a mere ghoul?<br /> On the other hand, a ghoul werewolf can threate to behead disobedient vampires during the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-27T08:32:01-08:00","id":1426318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world